{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore","id":1052659,"title":"No, you really ARE just a monster! (Reflection on the nature of Lore)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-21T11:43:39-08:00","id":1052659,"title":"No, you really ARE just a monster! (Reflection on the nature of Lore)","content":"So, there are two ways to approach Lore. The bit that comes at the start of the book or splat or tribe or clan or set of powers or sect. The bit said in a matter-of-fact tone that creates the world for you, the mythos. One is the This Is True approach. Gaia argued with the first Werefox and frenzied. The Werespiders are the offspring of one of the Weaver's daughters. Each Breed was created to fulfill a certain task for Gaia, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> The other approach is This Is Believed. This is the origin this group thinks is true. This is what 1 dot in &quot;Ananasi Lore&quot; gets you. For a VTM example, the Arhimane Bloodline harks back to a 4th Generation Vampire who legends paint as a Valkyrie, the daughter of a literal Viking Goddess. And when she died she was resurrected by her mother as an undead warrior. That simply cannot be 100% true, everyone reading that knows it isn't true. They are in reality (most likely) the result of Ennoia taking pity on a female Viking warrior (who she may have stalked for many years) who was crushed beneath a fallen building. The take-away (I am going somewhere with this) is that Adissa will have told the tale of how she was resurrected by her mother, a Goddess, but that isn't the this-is-what-happened fact.<br /> <br /> So, why am I posting here? Because the world of Werewolf is full of lore inherited not just from oral tradition, but from spirits. The Ahrimane Neonate is told the tale of Adissa and the weak King Ahrimane, but they don't feel the story, it doesn't call out to them, the spirits of the earth don't whisper it to them. To a Werewolf, Wereraven, Werecat, the lore of their people is a palpable and REAL thing. And if you take the first approach, everything that the Changing Breeds do is justified. If you take the second... things get messy. Very quickly.<br /> <br /> For absolute basics, Gaia created the Changing Breeds to carry out certain tasks, and while those tasks aren't all pretty (assassination of the worst, picking off the weak, limiting the growth of populations through devouring food and spreading disease) they are necessary and they promote harmony in the biosphere. Taken at face value, it has a nice harmony to it.<br /> <br /> The issue is that when we look at the lore of the Garou, Gurahl, Ananasi and Ratkin as a story passed down by people, animals and spirits (we'll get to them), things stop really working properly. The Ratkin have an ancestral memory + oral tradition (from here on I'll call it a Recalling) of being tasked with limiting the growth of human populations. The Garou have a Recalling of being made into Gaia's warriors. But can the Recalling be trusted?<br /> <br /> Oral Tradition and &quot;Religion&quot; (I know some of you cringe when that word is used to describe the spiritual relationship of the Garou with their role in life, but it's a fitting comparison) are non-starters. They simply aren't accurate. Historical Fact becomes Historical Story, a Historical Story becomes a Story. Chinese whispers. A population of humans can't keep stories going for a few thousand years, so wolf/human populations can't keep stories going for millenia.<br /> <br /> This is where spirits become important. They spread the tales, keep the Renown system going, and keep a more &quot;accurate&quot; oral history. How lovely and convenient. You just have to love these spirits. Teaching us everything we need to survive, telling us everything we need to know to keep doing those things we do. This feels... convenient.<br /> <br /> This is where we get into some existential problems. In a world where Magical Illusions exist, where memories are altered by the roll of a dicepool, is the collective memory of a group of Spirits something we trust? In a world where powerful beings can command spirits to obey their will with relative ease, do we feel comfortable (as a Wolf having just undergone the First Change in isolation) taking the word of this kind spirit?<br /> <br /> &quot;Your family live in the woods and the wilds. I'm here to guide you. Here is your history. Here is a list of rules you have to follow. Here is your purpose. Here are some powers which will become stronger IF you play by the rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, when you look at it like that, Renown, Honour, Succor, Wisdom... they get less and less comfortable. The Spirits who spread these tales, if they were compromised... if the rules were made up long ago by some outside force...<br /> <br /> Here's an &quot;Alternative History&quot; of the Changing Breeds which might as well be true with the information we have and the world as it is now in W20. This isn't a head-canon or fan theory, it's for demonstrative purposes only.<br /> <br /> Lilith. The first woman, the one who stole the True Name of divinity itself, cursed to never be loved. The mother of Monsters. The mother of Ennoia, who according to one (equally untrustworthy) bit of Gangrel lore popped out the first Werewolf after sleeping with a Wolf. Lilith, who (again, according to unreliable &quot;This Is What Is Believed&quot; lore) has the power to make monsters to suit her purposes. The power to command spirits. The power to grant people supernatural powers (just look at Caine and every Vampire from then on). Lilith, who had a score to settle with the ungrateful race of Cainites and the Children of Eve. Tell me, what is to stop her from turning animals into human-like monsters, or humans into animal-like monsters? What is to stop her from teaching them powers, or gifts? What is to stop her from making Spirits whose task is to lie and keep a status quo?<br /> <br /> It's fine that you're killing that little disabled child. It's fine that you spread that flu which killed that overgrown village. It's fine that you killed that coterie of Vampires. It's your purpose. It's what you were made for. Have some Renown. Good boy! Well done! Oh, and here's some pretty new Gifts you can learn...<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this is true, or that it should be true. I'm trying to make a comment on the nature of lore and how we should use it. I'm trying to point out why in-universe and out-of-universe skepticism of the status quo should be given more time and space. After all, it would be terrifying if any of the Garou lore was just bullshit spread by lying spirits. That might make them <i>monsters</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:07:14-08:00","id":1052679,"title":"","content":"That's like the number one thing I try and tell players as a preface before the game starts &quot; All this fluffy stuff is cool and all but don't get it twisted....your a monster....and you will probably do monsterous things&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:17:29-08:00","id":1052685,"title":"","content":"For anyone who actually likes the Lilith thing, the number 1 questions is &quot;why?&quot;. Well here's some ideas.<br /> <br /> - Vengeance against Cainites. Caine kind of screwed her over, and she grew up in a &quot;sins of the father&quot; type of world. If she created the Gifts and the Renown Systems, she can make the Changing Breeds a nightmare for Vampires to deal with.<br /> <br /> - Vengeance against the descendants of Adam and Eve. Adam was a rapist. Eve was a passive fool.<br /> <br /> - Vengeance against God. You think you're the Master of creation? I'm going to improve on your design! Can your species do THIS?! <i>wolf turns into 9 foot tall bipedal wolf</i><br /> <br /> - Morbid Curiosity. She's the mother of monsters. She has the power to do it. Why wouldn't she?<br /> <br /> And the one I actually like:<br /> <br /> - Ethics. Her entire philosophy is that pain is the best teacher. God gave her a world of nothing but pain. She was raped by Adam and cast out. She was abandoned by Lucifer and by Caine. The three archangels beat and (in some translations) raped her. She learnt from it and she realised that pain was the gateway to power. Only by getting burnt do we learn to not touch the stove. Only through revenge do we teach wrongdoers the true nature of the world. The races of the Changing breeds were created to make the world a more painful place. Hence Rage, Frenzying, and the morbid and arguably evil roles of many of the breeds. Hence there being so little infrastructure to keep harmony between the breeds. Why should Lilith care if the Wolves attack the others? It will teach them valuable lessons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-21-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:32:26-08:00","id":1052891,"title":"","content":"Garou predate the Kindred (Fera predate the Kindred by hundreds of millions of years). From the Garou perspective, the Kindred popped into existence five thousand years ago and are probably declscended from exiles from the High Umbra. The Garou would probably be sympathetic to Lilith and would probably help Lilith ash the entire Kindred race if it did not distract them from their mission to save the world (and they might go out of their way to ash Gangrel for their blasphemous claims about the origin of the Garou).<br /> <br /> Garou are nor 'monsters', they are the supernatural entities that you get to kill monsters. Yes, their ancestors practiced genocide against the European, American, and Australian Fera. Let us not be casting stones though because I can guarantee that the vast majority of people on the forum are probably descended from someone who helped commit genocide.<br /> <br /> In addition, this is a VtM thread, so it should be moved there. The origins of the Fera are canon in WtA, and Lilith has nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:41:24-08:00","id":1052895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052891#post1052891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou predate the Kindred (Fera predate the Kindred by hundreds of millions of years). From the Garou perspective, the Kindred popped into existence five thousand years ago and are probably declscended from exiles from the High Umbra. The Garou would probably be sympathetic to Lilith and would probably help Lilith ash the entire Kindred race if it did not distract them from their mission to save the world (and they might go out of their way to ash Gangrel for their blasphemous claims about the origin of the Garou).<br /> <br /> Garou are nor 'monsters', they are the supernatural entities that you get to kill monsters. Yes, their ancestors practiced genocide against the European, American, and Australian Fera. Let us not be casting stones though because I can guarantee that the vast majority of people on the forum are probably descended from someone who helped commit genocide.<br /> <br /> In addition, this is a VtM thread, so it should be moved there. The origins of the Fera are canon in WtA, and Lilith has nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a comment on the nature of Lore and how it should be used in-game, primarily focused on the WtA lore. I use examples from VtM because I know a lot about it, to make points about the WtA lore, which is unique as it has the benefit of being supported by spirits.<br /> <br /> The Werewolves and other Fera predating Vampirism by a long period is only knowable via the information Werewolves get from spirits. And the origins of the Fera aren't really cemented as canon, since as always the lore is in &quot;this is what is believed&quot; territory, which is the sensible and accurate approach to reading lore IMO. I give the example of the Werefoxes + Werecats (they can't BOTH be the youngest) and the Ahrimane (no, you can't be a Cainite and be a Zombie brought back by a Viking Goddess) since it demonstrates what Lore really is; the Lore of a group, their collective 'history' which is dubious at best.<br /> <br /> And like I say, the idea of Lilith creating the Fera is just an idea which I felt was relevant. Since her biological daughter canonically (as I say, is believed to have) popped out a Lupine. From what modern Werewolves and Fera see and hear, they could have originated 5000 years ago via the magic of Lilith, simply being the descendants of Lilith rather than Eve. That's my point. They could also be the work of an Archmage, or just a natural phenomena. What I'm saying, overall, is that we can never take lore at face value and we shouldn't view it as concrete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:58:16-08:00","id":1052907,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case...<br /> <br /> *Plot Twist*<br /> <br /> Lilith &amp; Caine never existed but are Ananasis who just tried some magic in the wrong place &amp; bam you got Vampires.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every splat have an explanation to what the other are.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary,and in the end the ST decide, and Vampires history is probably just as innacurate as the Werewolve's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:05:46-08:00","id":1052913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052907#post1052907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in that case...<br /> <br /> *Plot Twist*<br /> <br /> Lilith &amp; Caine never existed but are Ananasis who just tried some magic in the wrong place &amp; bam you got Vampires.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every splat have an explanation to what the other are.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary,and in the end the ST decide, and Vampires history is probably just as innacurate as the Werewolve's</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that I'm supposed to hate that, but it's actually quite cool. The Ananasi are blood-drinkers, and I can see a group of powerful Ananasi who are Wyrm-tainted making a deal with the Wyrm and it going wrong, and boom you get Vampires. If I were playing a Chronicle which built that up effectively I would actually be 100% onboard with that. I mean Mage posits at some point that the Antedeluvians were 13 Mages who botched a Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:19:11-08:00","id":1052923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052913#post1052913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing that I'm supposed to hate that, but it's actually quite cool. The Ananasi are blood-drinkers, and I can see a group of powerful Ananasi who are Wyrm-tainted making a deal with the Wyrm and it going wrong, and boom you get Vampires. If I were playing a Chronicle which built that up effectively I would actually be 100% onboard with that. I mean Mage posits at some point that the Antedeluvians were 13 Mages who botched a Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha ha I wasn't aiming at anyone to hate it ^^<br /> <br /> It's just that most of the time, people see the things from the scope of &quot;their&quot; main splat, while their is so many cool possibilities like that!<br /> <br /> For example I seem to remember the Changeling thinking that Vampires could come from a cursed/degenrated Redcap or something...<br /> <br /> My take on this is that no one actually really knows &amp; everything prior to Dark Age is mostly speculation &amp; distorted memories, when I'm STing I adapt depending the story I want while trying to not make anything looks like canon to the players ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:44:52-08:00","id":1052939,"title":"","content":"So quite a bit of your argument gets shot down simply because the non IC sections of the books say things work the way they do. This isn't IC lore. This isn't up for debate. The world is what it is because the writers are telling you (the reader) that some things just are the way they are. Now to address some of your points on IC lore.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore#post1052659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, why am I posting here? Because the world of Werewolf is full of lore inherited not just from oral tradition, but from spirits. The Ahrimane Neonate is told the tale of Adissa and the weak King Ahrimane, but they don't feel the story, it doesn't call out to them, the spirits of the earth don't whisper it to them. To a Werewolf, Wereraven, Werecat, the lore of their people is a palpable and REAL thing. And if you take the first approach, everything that the Changing Breeds do is justified. If you take the second... things get messy. Very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's a good thing that in the WtA setting (OOC) things work the first way then huh?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore#post1052659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The issue is that when we look at the lore of the Garou, Gurahl, Ananasi and Ratkin as a story passed down by people, animals and spirits (we'll get to them), things stop really working properly. The Ratkin have an ancestral memory + oral tradition (from here on I'll call it a Recalling) of being tasked with limiting the growth of human populations. The Garou have a Recalling of being made into Gaia's warriors. But can the Recalling be trusted?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Blood Memory. And yes, it can in fact be reliable. We know this because it works. Every Ratkin automatically knows every other Ratkin because they are all in their racial memory. So as least for recent history, we know it absolutely works. Not everything for Fera is based on oral tradition. The Mokole are the best example, since their purpose is literally to be the memory. The Kitsune are functionally immortal (the nine tails, assuming she isn't full on Incarna, has a current lifespan of about 20,000+ years). The Rokea don't die of old age either, so there's that. Ananasi can also extend their lifespans. And you have pre-history Gurahl waking up. All of the examples run contrary to your view of the setting.<br /> Oh, and Garou get Ancestors to channel and literally relive the memories of Garou from the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore#post1052659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here's an &quot;Alternative History&quot; of the Changing Breeds which might as well be true with the information we have and the world as it is now in W20. This isn't a head-canon or fan theory, it's for demonstrative purposes only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your alternate history approach is somewhat nonsensical. You've made Lilith out to be all powerful and able to manipulate spirits (and all of the Umbra) in an effort to trick the Fera into doing what they do. But again, the books say that this isn't the case. I suppose that yes, if you created your own all powerful being you could decide that all of history has been a trick and that the Garou are nothing but fooled monsters. But you are very much just making up whatever you want and rationalizing it by saying that everyone has been tricked and no one can see through it because....your all powerful being says so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052895#post1052895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Werewolves and other Fera predating Vampirism by a long period is only knowable via the information Werewolves get from spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And memories and actual living creatures saying so. And most importantly, the setting saying so (elaborated on below).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052895#post1052895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the origins of the Fera aren't really cemented as canon, since as always the lore is in &quot;this is what is believed&quot; territory, which is the sensible and accurate approach to reading lore IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you ignore the OOC parts of the setting that disagree with your approach.<br /> For example, we know a few hundred million years ago there were Mokole and Ananasi and Rokea (because they are the setting choices laid out for us). That predates Vampire. You can't really argue against that. If you can, I'd be interested what you have to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052895#post1052895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I give the example of the Werefoxes + Werecats (they can't BOTH be the youngest)</div> </div> </div> </div>This does at least support your claims. They can't be. But the Bastet <i>could have been</i> until the Kitsune were born. And since the Kitsune are hidden away (granted, baddly, since they're &quot;hidden&quot; on the largest continent) the Bastet as a whole don't know about them. This really just makes the Bastet mistaken. It doesn't contradict the setting as a whole at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052895#post1052895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I'm saying, overall, is that we can never take lore at face value and we shouldn't view it as concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can when the writers tell us about how the setting works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:06:08-08:00","id":1052949,"title":"","content":"In my games, 3th-bellow generations vampires are a non-thing. No real things. Actually, they exist, but are Umbral spirits that have all vanished long ago. My wife is annoying, gotta go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:57:24-08:00","id":1053062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052939#post1052939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quite a bit of your argument gets shot down simply because the non IC sections of the books say things work the way they do. This isn't IC lore. This isn't up for debate. The world is what it is because the writers are telling you (the reader) that some things just are the way they are. Now to address some of your points on IC lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost everything in CWoD canon is up for debate, sinceven that's how much of it is contradicted by another part of canon. I can't make much sense out of Werewolf canon unless I take everything as an unreliable narrator, even if it's out of character. This is because I don't know what to do with a statement about the setting if I can't figure out how I could verify it from within the setting.<br /> <br /> If I'm not a Muslim, and it seems to me that my Werewolf character would have as much difficulty proving to my satisfaction that the Triat literally exist in his world as a Muslim would have convincing me that Allah exists, it seems to me that it would be rational for my character to be more skeptical about the Triat. <br /> <br /> The OOC theological statements don't seem useful to me in a roleplaying game, because they don't help me put myself in my character's shoes and explore the setting from his perspective. I don't want to have to pat my character on the head and tell him &quot;there there, book says so every time Triatic dogma doesn't make sense to him.<br /> <br /> But hey, I'm just a filthy heretic whose favorite sourcebook is <u>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</u>. All the haters missed the point. This was the book that pioneered the in-setting rumors list before <u>Unknown Armies</u> did it. The point wasn't that Vicissitude was an alien virus. The point was that it could be, and how would your character know? What's given in the books is the tip of an iceberg infinitely more complex ando bizarre. If everything has to conform with the players' initial expectations until the end, where's the horror?<br /> <br /> But most fans eschew DSotBH because they find it silly, along with many other parts of canon I like. Well, I also prefer to disregard parts of canon I find silly.<br /> <br /> You know what I find silly? Looking at these tribes of ill-tempered, reactionary brutes who treat their kinfolk like breeding stock and have a long history of genocidal tendencies, magical gifts from powerful spirit allies, and globe-spanning political structures that have survived for millennia, you're and letting them convince you that no, really, they're the persecuted ones. They're the real heroes here because, if you believe their side of the story, The Enemy is a bajillion times worse.<br /> <br /> Oh, yes, the know they were so wrong when they said the other shifters were universally irredeemable wyrm-tainted degenerates, and when they said the New World tribes were universally irredeemable wyrm-tainted degenerates, and when they said the Bunyip were universally irredeemable wyrm-tainted degenerates. The Garou are super sorry about that stuff. But really, you've gotta believe them, the Black Spiral Dancers are such universally irredeemable Wyrm-tainted degenerates, you don't even know! You'd better be glad you don't, too, because even bothering to ask a Black Spiral Dancer why he joined or what it's like would be too dangerous! Aren't you glad you were warned before you made any attempt to get an inside perspective?<br /> <br /> And yeah, I guess this does have a little bit to do with the Black Spiral Dancers' transgressions against the Garou Nation's draconian sexual mores. Actually, it has a lot to do with that. But you've gotta understand, breaking the First Litany is really more like incest than homosexuality. Actually, it's not much more similar to either then they are to each other. But still, come on, eew! Think of the poor deformed metis babies! Just don't bother asking the majority of the metis what they think, because they've walked the Black Spiral for some stupid reason.<br /> <br /> And besides, the Black Spirals are into cannibalism and rape and pedophilia, too! That frat has way worse of a rape culture than anyone in the Garou Nation, the girls all say so. The Get of Fenris are perfect gentlemen who only make consensual Primal Urge checks.<br /> <br /> I can't take all that seriously if we're never going to get Tribebook: BSDs and see a real inside perspective that explains their motivations logically without making them less evil, as was done with the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T00:32:57-08:00","id":1053087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052939#post1052939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quite a bit of your argument gets shot down simply because the non IC sections of the books say things work the way they do. This isn't IC lore. This isn't up for debate. The world is what it is because the writers are telling you (the reader) that some things just are the way they are. Now to address some of your points on IC lore.<br /> <br /> Well it's a good thing that in the WtA setting (OOC) things work the first way then huh?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's Blood Memory. And yes, it can in fact be reliable. We know this because it works. Every Ratkin automatically knows every other Ratkin because they are all in their racial memory. So as least for recent history, we know it absolutely works. Not everything for Fera is based on oral tradition. The Mokole are the best example, since their purpose is literally to be the memory. The Kitsune are functionally immortal (the nine tails, assuming she isn't full on Incarna, has a current lifespan of about 20,000+ years). The Rokea don't die of old age either, so there's that. Ananasi can also extend their lifespans. And you have pre-history Gurahl waking up. All of the examples run contrary to your view of the setting.<br /> Oh, and Garou get Ancestors to channel and literally relive the memories of Garou from the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your alternate history approach is somewhat nonsensical. You've made Lilith out to be all powerful and able to manipulate spirits (and all of the Umbra) in an effort to trick the Fera into doing what they do. But again, the books say that this isn't the case. I suppose that yes, if you created your own all powerful being you could decide that all of history has been a trick and that the Garou are nothing but fooled monsters. But you are very much just making up whatever you want and rationalizing it by saying that everyone has been tricked and no one can see through it because....your all powerful being says so.<br /> <br /> <br /> And memories and actual living creatures saying so. And most importantly, the setting saying so (elaborated on below).<br /> Except that you ignore the OOC parts of the setting that disagree with your approach.<br /> For example, we know a few hundred million years ago there were Mokole and Ananasi and Rokea (because they are the setting choices laid out for us). That predates Vampire. You can't really argue against that. If you can, I'd be interested what you have to say.<br /> <br /> <br /> This does at least support your claims. They can't be. But the Bastet <i>could have been</i> until the Kitsune were born. And since the Kitsune are hidden away (granted, baddly, since they're &quot;hidden&quot; on the largest continent) the Bastet as a whole don't know about them. This really just makes the Bastet mistaken. It doesn't contradict the setting as a whole at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> We can when the writers tell us about how the setting works.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: That's all lore, it's up for debate. VTM talks about the 1st, 2nd and 3rd Generations as though they're &quot;this definitely happened&quot; canon in the Corebook. But we all know that &quot;this definitely happened&quot; is bullshit. VTM players (well, the ones I associate with) are mature enough to know that maybe the ancient Vampires (the creatures who lie) might be lying, and maybe we can't trust The Book of Nod, (which, as it turns out, might be a forgery). By the same standards, maybe these helpful spirits who tell me where to go and spread the Renown system (guidelines to live by) and grant me Kewl Powerz when I play ball might be manipulating me a bit. Oh, you want that awesome new power? Here's exactly what you need to get it. Oh, that's unethical? Well... [Elder Dominate/Presence or equivalent] that's your purpose in life, don't you remember? Eating that little kid with a broken leg in the desert might have felt evil, but it's what you were born to do! Have some Renown!<br /> <br /> 2: Except it kind of does. You're doing Special Pleading here. I'll get onto it.<br /> <br /> 3: Except it can't in a world where illusions and magic exist. I'm aware of the Mokole, but while they are the Memory they don't share their Memory with others all that much (beyond giving tactical info to the Ravens). And people never dying doesn't matter in a world where memories can be altered, where people can lie. Plus remember that our own memories in our short lifespans are edited and rewritten (ask any respectable psychologist) to the point of being nearly useless. And you're trusting the angry shark to remember things from 10,000 years ago with clarity? Feels like &quot;it's right because it just feels right&quot; isn't going to cut it. People who are under the effects of supernatural emotional control often feel like everything is okay and natural.<br /> <br /> 4: The books don't present that story because no one of note believes it. It would be a bit odd if the book had a This is Something which might have happened and a This is what is believed and it's totally different. Every Corebook just presents what is believed by the Splat itself. Look at Demon. Seems factual. Except they all have no way of knowing if their memories of the First War (which are Patchy at best) are real. What if they never were angels? What if they were created just to suffer? Doubt creeps in... As for Lilith, are you doubting her power levels? Now sure, you can't trust the Bahari Lore, but if Lilith does exist and her power is anything approximating that presented in her lore, she's one of the most powerful beings in existence.<br /> <br /> 5: We know that it is believed that the Rokea, Ananasi etc. date back to that time. And we know that it is believed that Vampires only date back to 5000 years ago. Can we trust either? No. Of course we can't. It's all common belief passed down by (possibly and in some cases definitely) inaccurate oral, blood and spiritual tradition.<br /> <br /> 6: They're wrong! Well done. They're just wrong about who is the youngest. Shame that none of the ancient lore is truly OOC and truly objective, when you scrutinize things or approach it the way (I think) it should be approached.<br /> <br /> 7: They tell you the tale of the Fera and the Werewolves. The story that pins up the game and the setting. It is my opinion that there are a billion and one possible origins which could lead to Garou being the way they are today, and thinking what they think. And when you take the second approach (which is backed up by repeated contradictions in Lore within books, between books and between Liines) you can't, you can't really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T04:33:02-08:00","id":1053130,"title":"","content":"Let us get one thing clear first, Black Spiral Dancers aren't like the Sabbat. They are very much like Baali. They are very much like the Nephandi and the Shadow Court.<br /> <br /> Sabbat, no matter how monstrous, was still formed from ideaks of freedom and choice. BSDs were formed when a tribe on its last legs was tortured enough that they gave up. There is a reason why even Sabbat hunts the infernalists.<br /> <br /> More to the point of this thread,though. Comparing werewolf and vampire on the same princibles is pretty useless, because they are two very different games with very different tones.<br /> <br /> A vampire is bound to the Jyhad, sure. But in a sense it is not a negative thing, just how vampires ARE. Gehenna has very little to do with the Jyhad. More than that, no vampire embraced is truly like another. Different clans can be worlds apart from one another. That is why there are so many splinter groups among them. And vampires generally combat to keep a hold of themselves, since you aren't born one.<br /> <br /> Being born a garou basically limits you to one duty, fighting for Gaia. You cannot ever escape what you are, you cannot ever choose to be anything but a garou. For the most part, all garou function almost identically. They all have the same powers, same weaknesses and same forms. The war the garou fight is also one that is horrible and very much the cause of the Apocalypse. Garou might have minor splinter groups, but in general they are all under the banner of the Nation.<br /> <br /> A garou can join the BSDs to avoid their fate, sure. But the lucky ones end up as food or breeders, those who manage to dance the spiral are forever basically slaves to the Wyrm (book of the Wyrm 20) and lose their autonomy somewhat.<br /> <br /> And in the end, it all comes down to the point I made in the other threat. No individual in WoD is a carbon copy of another. A Tzimisce can care a lot, a Child of Gaia can be a sociopath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T05:58:41-08:00","id":1053152,"title":"","content":"Yes, the idea that we need a BSD book so we can sympathize with rabid dogs is strange. In V20, the origins of the Kindred are presented as myth, and there are a few alternative myths presented (Kindred are demons, Set was the first Kindred, etc). In W20, there are no real alternative origin stories to the creation myths of each Fera, just different interpretations.<br /> <br /> If someone does not like the Lore, they can change it for their games, and I think that everyone does, to a lesser or greater degree. In my games, the Camarilla possesses a much more centralized organization, supported by a ghoul bureaucracy maintained by the elders of the Camarilla, and neonates who obey the elders of the Camarilla are granted lower generation through the use of a variant of From Marduk's Throat after centuries of service. In my games, all Mages are insane, it is just that the Marauders are powerful enough to warp reality with their insanity. In my games, the Week of Nightmares did not happen because of the actions of the Grand Alliance. I, however, do not expect anyone to follow or even like my changes to the Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:36:57-08:00","id":1053230,"title":"","content":"I'd say I'm a fan of the second approach for Vampire because I think that's a good part of the inherent conflict between the Sects. The ambiguity about Caine, the Antediluvians, the origin of Vampires, nature of their role/morality can fuel a fair bit of interesting story. It adds to that sort of horror. Whereas I feel that approach would make Werewolf less enjoyable. You don't need doubts about the nature of the Wyrm to have interest conflict between Garou and Pentex/BSD's. Or between the Changing Breeds and the Garou Nation. There is plenty of room for doubt and conflict (internal an external) without throwing their existence into question as well. Though, of course, might work for some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:01:14-08:00","id":1053247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053130#post1053130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...those who manage to dance the spiral are forever basically slaves to the Wyrm (book of the Wyrm 20) and lose their autonomy somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is important, because someone might glance through Book of the Wyrm and say 'nuh uh, the mean werewolves are about freedom!' because this is often what fallen Garou say themselves. W20 Black Spiral Dancers present their tribe as having freedom from the strictures of the Garou Nation, but in reality it is just a lie of the Wyrm. They aren't free to do whatever they want, since now they want what the Wyrm wants. Freedom to the BSDs just means they are free to commit whatever atrocities their black hearts desire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:04:59-08:00","id":1053249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053230#post1053230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say I'm a fan of the second approach for Vampire because I think that's a good part of the inherent conflict between the Sects. The ambiguity about Caine, the Antediluvians, the origin of Vampires, nature of their role/morality can fuel a fair bit of interesting story. It adds to that sort of horror. Whereas I feel that approach would make Werewolf less enjoyable. You don't need doubts about the nature of the Wyrm to have interest conflict between Garou and Pentex/BSD's. Or between the Changing Breeds and the Garou Nation. There is plenty of room for doubt and conflict (internal an external) without throwing their existence into question as well. Though, of course, might work for some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the whole point of Vampire seems to be somehow justifying your existence to yourself. Whether it is through Humanity, Paths, Camarilla or Sabbat or even Noddist lore. It makes sense to try to justify being a undead blood drinking monster by referring to a lineage of one.<br /> <br /> Garou,well, like I said above, they aren't as free to choose. Mages, Changelings, Vampires and I think even Wraiths can still choose more freely who they are and what they are. Garou basically have to grin and bear it or try to die gloriously if they don't like being one. Every one is -expected- to fight for Gaia in someway, otherwise they betray their people. That to me is one huge personal horror about them, not even that Garou Nation is a bad place, just that you are utterly stuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:22:56-08:00","id":1053262,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of good points already so instead of arguing in a coherent manner and potentially being redundant, I am just going to keep nattering about individual bits that got my neurons firing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1052939#post1052939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've made Lilith out to be all powerful and able to manipulate spirits (and all of the Umbra) in an effort to trick the Fera into doing what they do. But again, the books say that this isn't the case. I suppose that yes, if you created your own all powerful being you could decide that all of history has been a trick and that the Garou are nothing but fooled monsters. <b>But you are very much just making up whatever you want and rationalizing it by saying that everyone has been tricked and no one can see through it because....your all powerful being says so.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This sort of reminds me of Descartes' struggle to grasp the nature of reality. <i>How do we know anything? Are our senses lying to us? Is the the surrounding world some great big con, put on by some god-like deceiver? </i>Within the context of the game, that is basically what the Lillith idea is. It is not particularly revolutionary, interesting or cool to have every assumption about the setting be predicated on a lie; as far as devices go, that is both old hat <i>and </i>lame. It is very similar to the cliche 'it was all a dream' plot reveal, because once it turns out to be the case, all a character can really do is drop whatever (now irrelevant) thing they were doing and start playing by the new rules of the 'real world.'<br /> <br /> Rather than pulling the rug out from under your players, why not just choose to go with a setting premise that you are all comfortable with and stick with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-22-2017, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:24:40-08:00","id":1053263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053249#post1053249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the whole point of Vampire seems to be somehow justifying your existence to yourself. Whether it is through Humanity, Paths, Camarilla or Sabbat or even Noddist lore. It makes sense to try to justify being a undead blood drinking monster by referring to a lineage of one.<br /> <br /> Garou,well, like I said above, they aren't as free to choose. Mages, Changelings, Vampires and I think even Wraiths can still choose more freely who they are and what they are. Garou basically have to grin and bear it or try to die gloriously if they don't like being one. Every one is -expected- to fight for Gaia in someway, otherwise they betray their people. That to me is one huge personal horror about them, not even that Garou Nation is a bad place, just that you are utterly stuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this not scream Mind Control, Death Cult and Whoever Set This System Up Is Evil with an E? At least Vampires don't give a shit if one of their childer fucks off and never contacts them again.<br /> <br /> Like surely the personal horror of Werewolf would just be 1000x worse if not only are they stuck fighting this holy war, they're also completely wrong about cosmology. It would make it a comment on the failings of religions and extremism IRL. Also it would make the whole thing very bleak and tragic.<br /> <br /> For example, I did a Wraith twist where everyone ends up being destroyed by Oblivion. Everyone. Heaven? No. Oblivion. Hell? No. Oblivion. Wraith? For a time, maybe. Ascension? Ha! Oblivion. &quot;So... we just stop?&quot; becomes the bleak betrayal of the narrative. Done well it's incredible. Done poorly, your players will never speak to you again, so tread carefully. Luckily my players don't mind when I pull the rug from under them because it feels justifiable and suits an exciting (if grim) narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:33:00-08:00","id":1053270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053130#post1053130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let us get one thing clear first, Black Spiral Dancers aren't like the Sabbat. They are very much like Baali. They are very much like the Nephandi and the Shadow Court.<br /> <br /> Sabbat, no matter how monstrous, was still formed from ideaks of freedom and choice. BSDs were formed when a tribe on its last legs was tortured enough that they gave up. There is a reason why even Sabbat hunts the infernalists.<br /> <br /> More to the point of this thread,though. Comparing werewolf and vampire on the same princibles is pretty useless, because they are two very different games with very different tones.<br /> <br /> A vampire is bound to the Jyhad, sure. But in a sense it is not a negative thing, just how vampires ARE. Gehenna has very little to do with the Jyhad. More than that, no vampire embraced is truly like another. Different clans can be worlds apart from one another. That is why there are so many splinter groups among them. And vampires generally combat to keep a hold of themselves, since you aren't born one.<br /> <br /> Being born a garou basically limits you to one duty, fighting for Gaia. You cannot ever escape what you are, you cannot ever choose to be anything but a garou. For the most part, all garou function almost identically. They all have the same powers, same weaknesses and same forms. The war the garou fight is also one that is horrible and very much the cause of the Apocalypse. Garou might have minor splinter groups, but in general they are all under the banner of the Nation.<br /> <br /> A garou can join the BSDs to avoid their fate, sure. But the lucky ones end up as food or breeders, those who manage to dance the spiral are forever basically slaves to the Wyrm (book of the Wyrm 20) and lose their autonomy somewhat.<br /> <br /> And in the end, it all comes down to the point I made in the other threat. No individual in WoD is a carbon copy of another. A Tzimisce can care a lot, a Child of Gaia can be a sociopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just that all that just sounds way too much like IRL military/cult propaganda for me to take it seriously. &quot;You belong to us, you are nothing without us, the enemy are depraved lunatic cannibals worthy only of death because they didn't follow the right goddess and that's all you need to know, so stop asking stupid questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chanting &quot;This is what the book says!&quot; is different from explaining why my character should should believe it. Approaching canon as journalism is different from ignoring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:36:14-08:00","id":1053273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053270#post1053270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that all that just sounds way too much like IRL military/cult propaganda for me to take it seriously. &quot;You belong to us, you are nothing without us, the enemy are depraved lunatic cannibals worthy only of death because they didn't follow the right goddess and that's all you need to know, so stop asking stupid questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chanting &quot;This is what the book says!&quot; is different from explaining why my character should should believe it. Approaching canon as journalism is different from ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then go play Mage or some other game with more ambiguity. You don't have to like it, but them's the breaks. Werewolves are animistic spirit warriors. In order to fight a war, you need enemies. This is how the game is presented so you don't just sit there and constantly agonize over whether you even should be fighting. That is why the Garou have such an obvious clarity of purpose- you don't have to like it, but it is necessary in a game that is essentially all about visceral spiritual warfare.<br /> <br /> The premise breaks down, obviously, if you are constantly second-guessing yourself, your superiors, and the spirits.<br /> WtA stands for Werewolf the Apocalypse, not Werewolf the Anxiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-22-2017, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:39:55-08:00","id":1053276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053270#post1053270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that all that just sounds way too much like IRL military/cult propaganda for me to take it seriously. &quot;You belong to us, you are nothing without us, the enemy are depraved lunatic cannibals worthy only of death because they didn't follow the right goddess and that's all you need to know, so stop asking stupid questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chanting &quot;This is what the book says!&quot; is different from explaining why my character should should believe it. Approaching canon as journalism is different from ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take what you're saying about the BSDs and make it about Vampires and you have a compelling argument within the Lore. While someone could make the argument you're making, ask questions, with the BSDs they'd find &quot;oh, they actually ARE evil&quot;. Vampires are a whole other ball game, since plenty of them aren't how Werewolves think they are. Becoming a leading expert on Vampires among Werewolves would be a big help to the Nation without playing by its rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:46:54-08:00","id":1053285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053263#post1053263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does this not scream Mind Control, Death Cult and Whoever Set This System Up Is Evil with an E? At least Vampires don't give a shit if one of their childer fucks off and never contacts them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it doesn't to some garou? Heck, I have written a sub-faction of garou who want to destroy the Nation due to seeing it as evil.<br /> <br /> However, the reason it isn't evil is, that it sadly is 100% needed. Every garou, no matter if a metis that can't breed or a homid who had the instincts of a pug, is now needed for the world to be as good as it is now. Thanks to their ancestors spending way too much time in-fighting and arguing over differences.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't understand why everything has to be even more extremely bleak and tragic. The fact that the world is ending, nature is slowly being pushed to the point where animals no longer have any room but to disappear for human convenience, places are polluted out of greed and fast bucks, cultures are lost by their members assimilating to the mainstream culture and only one of those listed is fiction is frankly a lot of bleakness all ready. False faith really doesn't need to be added to the mix.<br /> <br /> Besides, calling religion totally wrong undercuts what is even worse than it being false. That people take the words of peace, of charity and love, and they twist them for hate. That those of truly and honestly want to help and follow the guidelines are overworked to death and jadedness by the amount of help people need. While those, who twist words and encourage violence, prosper.<br /> <br /> Darkness needs light to be dark, otherwise you are just watching shades of black.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:55:04-08:00","id":1053291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053270#post1053270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that all that just sounds way too much like IRL military/cult propaganda for me to take it seriously. &quot;You belong to us, you are nothing without us, the enemy are depraved lunatic cannibals worthy only of death because they didn't follow the right goddess and that's all you need to know, so stop asking stupid questions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chanting &quot;This is what the book says!&quot; is different from explaining why my character should should believe it. Approaching canon as journalism is different from ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, don't forget that there are 13 tribes and each one kinda thinks another can't do their job right. One even literally left the Nation because the others were not doing things 'right'. I'm not saying garou are blameless. In the end they are still monsters to humanity their morality, even if Gaia myth is correct. That is one aspect of horror about them.<br /> <br /> Honestly? Have FUN with your character questioning it all. That is good RP, and I enjoy playing contrary characters a lot myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:03:21-08:00","id":1053297,"title":"","content":"I think that it's important to reflect in the difference between OOC and IOC lore.<br /> <br /> IOC Lore (like the Book of Nod, which has notes from Beckett) it's &quot;what the characters believe&quot;. It just happens that most vampire books go with a Nodist approach (that Cain, or something like him, existed it's basically certain), and thus we assume that what the Book of Nod says it's mostly true.<br /> <br /> OOC Lore it's the Word of God. It's as up to debate as the wording of the rules, as it comes from the same source.<br /> <br /> To my understanding, saying that the OOC Lore of Werewolf that indicates what the Garou are and it's place in the cosmos it's up to debate has no more sense thatn saying that the rules to cause damage with a Katana are the opinion of an unreliable narrator<br /> <br /> Saying that, because the OOC Lore contradicts itself numerous times, then it's not certain but &quot;what an unreliable narrator believes&quot;, has as much sense to me as saying that, because the rules to cause damage with a given weapon varies between M20 and W20, then that damage represents what Mages and Werewolves wrongly believe about Katanas.<br /> <br /> IOC it's made to create mystery, OOC it's made to create a setting. IOC two characters may contradict each other, it just happens that one it's right and the other it's wrong (even if only God knows who). An OOC contradiction it's a real contradiciton (two authors that weren't on the same page, so to speak) and it's to be solved by the ST if ever comes into play (or if the ST wants, of course)<br /> <br /> The ST can take OOC and IOC as he wants. The ST can make Setites to be the only ones who know the Truth in vampire (and then will have to explain why nobody else's does), but this doesn't change the nature of OOC and IOC: When you change the OOC It's no longer an &quot;interpretation of the books&quot;, it's an intervention, a change of the material, even when it's done to fix a contradiction. Just as when you change the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:10:50-08:00","id":1053300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Except these books don't tell us which is which. We're left to guess. And I've come to realise that it's easiest when you see everything as IOC. So much is presented as OOC Lore, Word of God, and simply isn't true. Vicissitude was called an Alien Disease From the Umbra in no uncertain terms, for just one example.<br /> <br /> Rules are obviously different, since they don't stretch into the mists of time and they don't get debated in-universe. Rules are mechanics. There's a big difference between &quot;Gaia made the Changing Races and gave us all a task&quot; and &quot;roll Strength + 1 Lethal&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day it says it on the tin; Golden Rule, the Lore and setting and rules exist for us, not the other way around. I take that as a kind of endorsement as seeing everything as myths and legends and questioning everything. Hey, maybe this one myth is right, or half-right. That's way more interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> For example, in my current game I'm building up the idea of some Antedeluvians being children of Lilith rather than Eve. Ennoia, Malkav, Arikel, and the missing triplet of Malkav and Arikel, all Lilin offspring. Is it canon? That's a matter of opinion. It's stated as Word of God. I guess that makes it true. Except it definitely isn't Word of God. Do you see what I'm saying? The settings and lores are flexible. They're stories that are told to the Characters and Players, and some of those stories might be true. Go and find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:13:49-08:00","id":1053301,"title":"","content":"For me, it depends on what line the PCs play. As an ST, I put the PCs are the center of the universe and customize the game for the PCs. No PC is 100% correct about the setting.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are Garou, they the Werewolf lore will be the most, but not completely correct. <br /> <br /> If the PCs are Kindred, then Cain existed, though the Book of Nod doesn't tell the whole story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:37:42-08:00","id":1053313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, in my current game I'm building up the idea of some Antedeluvians being children of Lilith rather than Eve. Ennoia, Malkav, Arikel, and the missing triplet of Malkav and Arikel, all Lilin offspring. Is it canon? That's a matter of opinion. It's stated as Word of God. I guess that makes it true. Except it definitely isn't Word of God. Do you see what I'm saying? The settings and lores are flexible. They're stories that are told to the Characters and Players, and some of those stories might be true. Go and find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nop. What I get it's that you're confusing your freedom of making whatever you want with the OOC material, including stating that an almost ignored OOC section somewhere on Vampre it's right and the one assumed in most books it's wrong, with the idea that OOC it's &quot;what IOC character believe&quot; and wasn't written with a authoral authority. Which it's wrong, in truth, when OOC contradict, it's not that one is wrong and the other right, but a true contradiction, a paradox if you want.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Crusade was so assumed to be true, that you could play a Black Hand member and hunt actual trains of flesh infected with that virus. It had (and now has again) solid rules to it, as solid as Strength +1 to damage. For a moment, it was Canon. And probably, if you started your chronicle with Black Hand assuming that Vicissitude it's an alien diease, you ain't going to change your chronicle just because it's not canon anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:00:39-08:00","id":1053326,"title":"","content":"Something I thing is worth a note.<br /> <br /> Vampire can be played with looser lore easily, it isn't reliant on it. The vampires of VtM are still pretty much typical vampires.<br /> <br /> Without its lore, Werewolf loses most of its shine. There is a reason why some fans of werewolf movies don't like WtA, as it isn't as much about werewolves in the traditional sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:07:09-08:00","id":1053330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053263#post1053263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like surely the personal horror of Werewolf would just be 1000x worse if not only are they stuck fighting this holy war, they're also completely wrong about cosmology. It would make it a comment on the failings of religions and extremism IRL. Also it would make the whole thing very bleak and tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think it comes down to intentional splat themes. Vampire has a lot of tools and intent for existential horror and identity crisis. Morality, Humanity, numerous Paths, numerous conflicting sects, various conflicting historical accounts. Turmoil over one's existence and place in the world is a huge thing. To me, Werewolf doesn't question the nature of the conflict, it is designed to be about how one pursues that conflict. I think it'd be inherently unfair to critisize your own lore alternatives because I don't want to put this as, 'this is a concept that would inherently be handled bad.' But to me it is a concept that is inherently unsatisfying in how Werewolf is presented as a game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:12:18-08:00","id":1053333,"title":"","content":"IOC should be different than OOC. Now, there is some ambiguity in every OOC. For example, in VtM, the 3rd generation could be refuges from the High Umbra, banished from their home realm in the High Umbra by Caine after they killed off the 2nd generation, and became the first generation of vampires when they permanently possessed human hosts. The Second City would have been created by the 3rd generation to mimic the First City of the High Umbra. There is nothing in particular in the books that conflict with that interpretation, and it helps to address some of the conflicts between the cosmologies of the various splats quite nicely, since the First City never existed on the Earth in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:27:12-08:00","id":1053338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053333#post1053333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and it helps to address some of the conflicts between the cosmologies of the various splats quite nicely, since the First City never existed on the Earth in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not trying to be argumentative. But what is the inherent cosmological issue between splats if the First city existed on Earth?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:31:16-08:00","id":1053341,"title":"","content":"Well, the conflict is primarily with WtA, since neither the Garou or the Ratkin, the two groups most likely to have infiltrated such a city, mention its existence. Since the Ratkin were tasked with controlling human populations, the First City would have been a natural target for colonization for them (and for attacks by ancient Garou who would have freaked out when they discovered large groups of humans ruled by Wyrm creatures). In addition, the First City was destroyed by the Great Flood, which does not exist in the history of WtA to my knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:41:37-08:00","id":1053350,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053341#post1053341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the conflict is primarily with WtA, since neither the Garou or the Ratkin, the two groups most likely to have infiltrated such a city, mention its existence. Since the Ratkin were tasked with controlling human populations, the First City would have been a natural target for colonization for them (and for attacks by ancient Garou who would have freaked out when they discovered large groups of humans ruled by Wyrm creatures). In addition, the First City was destroyed by the Great Flood, which does not exist in the history of WtA to my knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wasn't there a story that part of the downfall of Enoch was due to Garou attacks? Things get especially tricky with all that pre-history stuff, though, I'd say. But I appreciate the point of view on this one. I think if there was ever one dubious aspect of the Book of Nod, it was the Flood. Which could honestly be written off as regional instead of world-wide. Always had the inner view that this was after the Impergium ended, localized in the Middle East/Fertile Crescent/etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:00:54-08:00","id":1053359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053330#post1053330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think it comes down to intentional splat themes. Vampire has a lot of tools and intent for existential horror and identity crisis. Morality, Humanity, numerous Paths, numerous conflicting sects, various conflicting historical accounts. Turmoil over one's existence and place in the world is a huge thing. To me, Werewolf doesn't question the nature of the conflict, it is designed to be about how one pursues that conflict. I think it'd be inherently unfair to critisize your own lore alternatives because I don't want to put this as, 'this is a concept that would inherently be handled bad.' But to me it is a concept that is inherently unsatisfying in how Werewolf is presented as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving that a like because it's respectful and it made me see it differently. I feel like I'm seeing Werewolf and thinking &quot;hmm, however can I make this a darker shade of grey&quot;. I will say that handled properly, theme of questioning conflict don't necessarily subtract from themes of how to handle conflict. My games have both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:03:39-08:00","id":1053361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053350#post1053350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a story that part of the downfall of Enoch was due to Garou attacks? Things get especially tricky with all that pre-history stuff, though, I'd say. But I appreciate the point of view on this one. I think if there was ever one dubious aspect of the Book of Nod, it was the Flood. Which could honestly be written off as regional instead of world-wide. Always had the inner view that this was after the Impergium ended, localized in the Middle East/Fertile Crescent/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flood could be a metaphor for God's wrath. I mean can you see even an Ancillae being killed by a flood? Bashing damage from water and rocks, lethal at worst, and if it wipes out the Vampires it 100% certainly kills all life. I'd say the &quot;flood&quot; is a metaphor for something else.<br /> <br /> Or the Book of Nod is a forgery by Saulot which fused common Judeo-Christian-Islamic religious tropes with Vampire myths to get a mass audience for his lies and help plant seeds of control in the Vampire consciousness (the &quot;thinbloods will rule over you&quot; stuff if just a method to make people kill thin-bloods and bring Gehenna sooner) and the truth is 100% unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:19:47-08:00","id":1053365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053361#post1053361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flood could be a metaphor for God's wrath. I mean can you see even an Ancillae being killed by a flood? Bashing damage from water and rocks, lethal at worst, and if it wipes out the Vampires it 100% certainly kills all life. I'd say the &quot;flood&quot; is a metaphor for something else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Possibly. For Kindred being killed, said flood lasted over a month and covered close to mountains? (Haven't read the Bible in a while). So lack of blood and time to deal damage could do it for a good number, possibly. I mean, wasn't it just Noah's family who survived anyway? But yeah, I do agree there are a lot of cool things it could be standing for instead of a literal flood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the Book of Nod is a forgery by Saulot which fused common Judeo-Christian-Islamic religious tropes with Vampire myths to get a mass audience for his lies and help plant seeds of control in the Vampire consciousness (the &quot;thinbloods will rule over you&quot; stuff if just a method to make people kill thin-bloods and bring Gehenna sooner) and the truth is 100% unknown. </div> </div> </div> I personally like the concept of Saulot just altering parts for a goal. But yeah, no flood at all could fit as well.<br /> <br /> And to again note on the post above this one, I think the concept of Garou being wrong could work. I think it would just work much better in say, a Vampire focused crossover. Because the way they are presented in V20 leaves a lot more room to play without getting into all the details of their splat at play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:28:23-08:00","id":1053368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053365#post1053365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Possibly. For Kindred being killed, said flood lasted over a month and covered close to mountains? (Haven't read the Bible in a while). So lack of blood and time to deal damage could do it for a good number, possibly. I mean, wasn't it just Noah's family who survived anyway? But yeah, I do agree there are a lot of cool things it could be standing for instead of a literal flood.<br /> <br /> I personally like the concept of Saulot just altering parts for a goal. But yeah, no flood at all could fit as well.<br /> <br /> And to again note on the post above this one, I think the concept of Garou being wrong could work. I think it would just work much better in say, a Vampire focused crossover. Because the way they are presented in V20 leaves a lot more room to play without getting into all the details of their splat at play.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with Garou being wrong in a Vampire-focused game is as follows:<br /> <br /> &quot;My religion is a lie&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampire PCs: &quot;oh... okay. Fine. I guess.&quot; *pats on back*<br /> <br /> The story of an NPCs entire culture being bullshit isn't compelling stuff. It just reaffirms that age-old trope of the White Man turning up at the culture of the Other and revealing that their Gods are fake or their religion is a lie or their system is corrupt and they're all being deceived. The culture of the Garou being wrong is only a blow to the players if they're deeply invested. I would only do a &quot;haha it's all a forgery&quot; in a Noddist game (Path of Caine vampire Frenzies, Bahari shrugs and says that the Dark Mother's gifts are more metaphysical than anything and that erroneous lore can still bring enlightenment) where the players have studied the lore and chased whispers and are deeply invested. Same with the Garou twist of &quot;oh you fools, you're just the result of one of Lilith's daughters being a perve and letting a fucking Wolf stick its dick in her&quot; (said more tactfully).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:35:08-08:00","id":1053371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053368#post1053368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue with Garou being wrong in a Vampire-focused game is as follows:<br /> <br /> &quot;My religion is a lie&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampire PCs: &quot;oh... okay. Fine. I guess.&quot; *pats on back*<br /> <br /> The story of an <b>NPCs</b> entire culture being bullshit isn't compelling stuff. It just reaffirms that age-old trope of the White Man turning up at the culture of the Other and revealing that their Gods are fake or their religion is a lie or their system is corrupt and they're all being deceived. The culture of the Garou being wrong is only a blow to the players if they're deeply invested. I would only do a &quot;haha it's all a forgery&quot; in a Noddist game (Path of Caine vampire Frenzies, Bahari shrugs and says that the Dark Mother's gifts are more metaphysical than anything and that erroneous lore can still bring enlightenment) where the players have studied the lore and chased whispers and are deeply invested. Same with the Garou twist of &quot;oh you fools, you're just the result of one of Lilith's daughters being a perve and letting a fucking Wolf stick its dick in her&quot; (said more tactfully).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my thought was more, group of players both Werewolf and Vampire in a common cause discovering messed up reality after setting aside their differences. I agree it has to be an established focus. I just felt cross-over worked better because (obviously) the much of Werewolf is watered down to fit Vampire. So it'd probably have to be something important for both groups to feel that way. It, of course, really depends on the specific character/plot being presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:39:09-08:00","id":1053401,"title":"","content":"Wow, this thread went a long way in the day I was gone.<br /> Read through everything and handed out likes for posts I agree with. A lot of the stuff has been covered so I will try and just respond to some specific things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053062#post1053062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Almost everything in CWoD canon is up for debate, sinceven that's how much of it is contradicted by another part of canon. I can't make much sense out of Werewolf canon unless I take everything as an unreliable narrator, even if it's out of character. This is because I don't know what to do with a statement about the setting if I can't figure out how I could verify it from within the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can take that stance I suppose. (as an example) From that point of view, the Wyrm might not even exist. But we know, OOC that it does because the books tell us very clearly it does. The characters can see it all around them in game. They have specific powers that tell them it does and powers to cleanse it. If you question the Setting on that level, it leaves the entire discussion kind of moot because you can just make up whatever you like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053087#post1053087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3: Except it can't in a world where illusions and magic exist. I'm aware of the Mokole, but while they are the Memory they don't share their Memory with others all that much (beyond giving tactical info to the Ravens). And people never dying doesn't matter in a world where memories can be altered, where people can lie. Plus remember that our own memories in our short lifespans are edited and rewritten (ask any respectable psychologist) to the point of being nearly useless. And you're trusting the angry shark to remember things from 10,000 years ago with clarity? Feels like &quot;it's right because it just feels right&quot; isn't going to cut it. People who are under the effects of supernatural emotional control often feel like everything is okay and natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Rank 1 Gift for perfect memory recall. But obviously the counterpoint to this is that it doesn't work and you can't trust it because: Magick exists. That logic shuts down any and all possible arguments that the Setting works as described by the authors. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053087#post1053087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 5: We know that it is believed that the Rokea, Ananasi etc. date back to that time. And we know that it is believed that Vampires only date back to 5000 years ago. Can we trust either? No. Of course we can't. It's all common belief passed down by (possibly and in some cases definitely) inaccurate oral, blood and spiritual tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are just kind of wrong here. There is a setting book for the age of dinosaurs. In that book, these are your Breed choices. It's fairly straight forward. Mokole, Ananasi and Rokea were around then. Because the authors (again) tell us they were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053263#post1053263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How does this not scream Mind Control, Death Cult and Whoever Set This System Up Is Evil with an E? At least Vampires don't give a shit if one of their childer fucks off and never contacts them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou are quite cult-like. I'm not arguing that at least. And &quot;evil&quot; is a mostly useless concept in the WoD. Spirals aren't the enemy because they're &quot;evil&quot;. They're the enemy because they are serving a force that wants the destruction/corruption of....everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053300#post1053300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the end of the day it says it on the tin; Golden Rule, the Lore and setting and rules exist for us, not the other way around. I take that as a kind of endorsement as seeing everything as myths and legends and questioning everything. Hey, maybe this one myth is right, or half-right. That's way more interesting to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are just going to invoke the Golden Rule to shut down discussion, what's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053300#post1053300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For example, in my current game I'm building up the idea of some Antedeluvians being children of Lilith rather than Eve. Ennoia, Malkav, Arikel, and the missing triplet of Malkav and Arikel, all Lilin offspring. Is it canon? That's a matter of opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. I think we may disagree on what &quot;canon&quot; means then. Just because something works for your personal game, doesn't in any way make it canon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:32:12-08:00","id":1053424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053401#post1053401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think we may disagree on what &quot;canon&quot; means then. Just because something works for your personal game, doesn't in any way make it canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so we are clear- canon is stuff that is in the published book sitting on my shelf- or idpersona's shelf, whoever- and that commonality is important. Canon is <i>not </i>stuff that happened or is happening in anyone else's game (not even Skemp's). You can have an opinion, but until I see a writer credit, you can't go around elevating your own stories to the level of canon. This isn't so we can be dicks about it either, but this is a WtA forum. The common factor is a game about hybrid shapeshifter shaman warriors in a fight at the end of the world. If that sounds stupid to you or if you want to alter that fundamentally, go ahead, but don't treat that like something we have to honor as valid in our own understanding of the baseline game.<br /> <br /> I honestly think a vampire game where the Garou are the twisted creations of Lillith works well. As a plot point in a werewolf game, I think it is kind of pants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-22-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:54:30-08:00","id":1053437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053401#post1053401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. I think we may disagree on what &quot;canon&quot; means then. Just because something works for your personal game, doesn't in any way make it canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is published work which states that as Word of God. Arikel and Malkav being children of Lilith and having a sibling, and them being part of the Clan Curses. Are you trying to misread what I write?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, I can see that someone who didn't know that bit of Lore could read what I wrote either way.<br /> <br /> My point is that something which is presented as Word of God is still optional because it's ALL optional. I don't enjoy invoking the Golden Rule since it isn't something that you normally need to say, it's just something that most people accept and are happy with, it's a rare occasion when it actually needs to be stated that the lore and rules exist for your use and that &quot;canon&quot; is a nebulous concept at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:06:59-08:00","id":1053450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053424#post1053424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think a vampire game where the Garou are the twisted creations of Lillith works well. As a plot point in a werewolf game, I think it is kind of pants.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a nice fluffy enjoyable ride where things happen as expected and the world &quot;plays fair&quot; with the beliefs of the players, that's cool. But there is something to be said for a world which fundamentally subverts the deeply held beliefs of the players. Take a look at Undertale for an example [spoilers ahead]. The very mechanics are a comment on the nature of Players happily engaging in murder to level up, gain HP and LV (levels of violence) and EXP (Execution Points). You're told off for doing the things you just do in RPGs. A Werewolf game where the Gift/Renown system is &quot;if you allow us to manipulate your behaviour we'll let you get stronger&quot; and their origin is dark and evil and their beliefs about having special roles are all bullshit is something similar. A comment on the dark nature of Player Mindset in TTRPG, the gullibility of the indoctrinated and the power of a carefully designed Propaganda State. It would also be a game full of despair, denial and both players and characters rejecting the very suggestion of it being true, rejecting the messenger and killing them even (acting exactly as you would predict, and as people do in real life when their indoctrinated views are challenged).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:19:57-08:00","id":1053461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore#post1052659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there are two ways to approach Lore. The bit that comes at the start of the book or splat or tribe or clan or set of powers or sect. The bit said in a matter-of-fact tone that creates the world for you, the mythos. One is the This Is True approach. Gaia argued with the first Werefox and frenzied. The Werespiders are the offspring of one of the Weaver's daughters. Each Breed was created to fulfill a certain task for Gaia, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> The other approach is This Is Believed. This is the origin this group thinks is true. This is what 1 dot in &quot;Ananasi Lore&quot; gets you.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this is true, or that it should be true. I'm trying to make a comment on the nature of lore and how we should use it. I'm trying to point out why in-universe and out-of-universe skepticism of the status quo should be given more time and space. After all, it would be terrifying if any of the Garou lore was just bullshit spread by lying spirits. That might make them <i>monsters</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back at my OP, I really can't imagine anything more inoffensive. Like seriously, these aren't controversial or crazy views on Lore. They're a mature approach (the approach most STs end up using in my experience) to dealing with Word of God, foundations of setting and individual origins of different groups. And I don't even think that any of the people commenting negatively necessarily even disagree with me in a general sense, since the responses have been Special Pleading for why it doesn't apply to <i>Werewolf</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:33:51-08:00","id":1053467,"title":"","content":"It is not pleading when we are talking about the basics of WtA. I doubt that VtM fans would be happy if a Mage fan declared that the Kindred were botched immortality experiments on the VtM forums or a Changeling fan said that Kindred were malformed Redcaps on the VtM forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:42:13-08:00","id":1053469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053467#post1053467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not pleading when we are talking about the basics of WtA. I doubt that VtM fans would be happy if a Mage fan declared that the Kindred were botched immortality experiments on the VtM forums or a Changeling fan said that Kindred were malformed Redcaps on the VtM forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>People have done that with the Mage thing, and some people resent Mage players attempting to shove everything into their Lore. I don't actually mind at all. It's interesting. Vampirism originating from 13 Mages botching a Magick roll to become Liches is a cool idea. You're assuming that I'm a hypocrite when I'm really not. I'm just trying to sell what I think is a more balanced and happy approach to Lore which results in better storytelling.<br /> <br /> If I were playing and an ST carefully set up and revealed any of the following, I would be perfectly down with it:<br /> <br /> - Vampires are Ananasi Gone Wrong<br /> - Vampires are Magick Gone Wrong<br /> - Vampires were created by the Egyptian Gods<br /> - Vampirism is a spiritual virus from the Umbra<br /> - Vampires were literally spawned from the Wyrm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2017, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:50:52-08:00","id":1053474,"title":"","content":"Why does WtA get to be the only game line with objective lore? Mind control and alteration exist in this world so perhaps things might not be exactly what they seem? It's the World of Darkness, not the World of Unambiguous Black and White Morality, the WoD was created so that players could live in a world of grey and play monsters that aren't necessarily good or evil by their very nature., If there's an objective good and bad in this game, then what's the fucking point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11716-pixiekillerein","name":"PixiekillerEin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:54:26-08:00","id":1053477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053474#post1053474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's an objective good and bad in this game, then what's the fucking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point? Simple.<br /> <br /> Choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:55:57-08:00","id":1053480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053477#post1053477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point? Simple.<br /> <br /> Choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I see you take the Fallout 3 aproach to player choice and morality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11716-pixiekillerein","name":"PixiekillerEin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:57:47-08:00","id":1053482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053480#post1053480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, I see you take the Fallout 3 aproach to player choice and morality</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, would you like to set off a nuke for absolutely no reason (and I don't really have any reason for you to want to do it either), or would you like to make the nuke safe (the obviously good choice which is Correct)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:59:46-08:00","id":1053483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053474#post1053474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does WtA get to be the only game line with objective lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise leans on it heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:01:17-08:00","id":1053484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053483#post1053483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The premise leans on it heavily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but like.... would adding nuance to that, the existence of mind control, the possibility that people are lying, not serve to improve it at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11716-pixiekillerein","name":"PixiekillerEin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:08:39-08:00","id":1053486,"title":"","content":"Well, the Garou regularly deal with entities too powerful to be mind-controlled by anything less powerful than Gaia herself, so they have an objective check on the memories and history. It is the World of Darkness, not the World of Grayness, so there are always objective 'evils', there are just no objective 'goods'. <br /> <br /> In WtA, the Garou are not an objective 'good', but the Wyrm is an objective 'bad'. Garou are epic heroes, so they cannot be objectively 'good', and they often have to choose between two 'objective' evils. That, however, does not mean they are supernatural serial killers, just that they live in a world with precious few simple answers.<br /> <br /> For example, a lost child stumbles onto a Garou moot. It is probably a safe bet that modern Garou will not kill the child (at least not with the people I have always played with), but they have to do something with her because they cannot just return her to her parents because of the Veil. <br /> <br /> Do they call upon a spirit to erase her memory? Do they send her to an Umbra Realm to become an Ephemera in service to their Totem? Do they adopt her into the Tribe? Do they take her to Baffin Island and let Gaia make the choice? Every choice has a cost and a risk associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:12:51-08:00","id":1053490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053484#post1053484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> but like.... would adding nuance to that, the existence of mind control, the possibility that people are lying, not serve to improve it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're asking for Doubt to be an element of the Lore, and that's an X-Rated Theme. Short answer; yes. Doubt is a great theme which serves to improve everything, whether the Lore is true or otherwise. It's one of the biggest and most realistic ways to generate conflict between people who agree with eachother. Me and James both agree that Nazism is bad, but can either of us be sure that Jim is a Nazi? If there were no doubt, there would be no meaningful or nuanced conflict. It would just be two people going after a literal Nazi after immediately agreeing to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:17:40-08:00","id":1053491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053484#post1053484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> but like.... would adding nuance to that, the existence of mind control, the possibility that people are lying, not serve to improve it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind control probably wouldn't add nuance to that. In fact, it would seem a cheap bit of rug-pulling on par with DSotBH. People lying? Lying about what, exactly? It would similarly be a cheap bit after all these years to say &quot;no, it was all a lie, go home and be angsty&quot;.<br /> <br /> Blind faith in something is bad, but I think that we may disagree as to what, exactly, constitutes blind faith. Trusting the spirits that live alongside you and which you've cultivated a working relationship isn't blind faith. Assuming that you can just Rage out on anyone you please and that, given your nature, it's perfectly fine? That's blind faith. Werewolf doesn't typically deal with massive internal conspiracies because it's very upfront with the fact that the predecessors of the protagonists have screwed up horribly. You can see it in the shape of the world and all the consequences of those past actions. Dominate need not apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:18:58-08:00","id":1053524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053484#post1053484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but like.... would adding nuance to that, the existence of mind control, the possibility that people are lying, not serve to improve it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>So at least for me, adding nuance is completely fine. Saying the Setting itself (and authors) is/are lying to you takes a great deal away from the game since you are removing the foundation it's built on.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with the concept of having characters disagree on the nature of the cosmological conflict (there are entire factions within the Garou Nation that having differing views, to say nothing of the expanded Fera Breeds). I do have a problem with the idea that the entire setting is a farce. Because then what is the point of playing the game if you start with the premise that everything the game is based on are lies?<br /> <br /> Oh, also worth clarifying maybe. I am speaking from purely a Werewolf game/Setting perspective. This has nothing (zero) to do with the greater World(s) of Darkness as a whole. How Vampires or Changelings or Demons, etc. view things and what themes are relevant to those games make no difference in my stance as it pertains to this thread/subject. Vampire has themes that reinforce the idea that everything is or can be a lie. That isn't the same premise as Werewolf. And both games can be enjoyed for various reasons. For me, I enjoy both games for their differing themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053437#post1053437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is published work which states that as Word of God. Arikel and Malkav being children of Lilith and having a sibling, and them being part of the Clan Curses. Are you trying to misread what I write?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, I can see that someone who didn't know that bit of Lore could read what I wrote either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I obviously read it differently. For what it counts, I try and approach all forum discussion in good faith.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on the rest of the post?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053437#post1053437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My point is that something which is presented as Word of God is still optional because it's ALL optional. I don't enjoy invoking the Golden Rule since it isn't something that you normally need to say, it's just something that most people accept and are happy with, it's a rare occasion when it actually needs to be stated that the lore and rules exist for your use and that &quot;canon&quot; is a nebulous concept at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some is, some isn't. Any information presenting IC is 100% option, because the IC bits in the books are meant to be flawed. If you have information given in a Setting section or a rules section, that's not so much up for debate. That's the authors telling you how the system or Setting work. And I fully recognize that some books (especially earlier ones) have writers that just don't understand the setting, or have a....non-traditional view of it. When something pops up in a book that goes against the basics of the Setting, you kind of <i>have to</i> write it off as nonsensical (Examples: a Vampire diablerizing a Garou; CoG revised; etc.). That is technically against canon, but that happens sometimes.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I would be less argumentative about this had it been presented from the get go as: This is my interesting idea for an alternative Setting for WtA. But you seemed to be arguing that this was completely within reason that everyone in the Setting is wrong and it's just that nobody knows it. And the foundation of the Setting is a lie. Spirits are wrong. The spirit world itself kind of has to follow as being a grand trick (since proof abounds there of the Setting's premises). All spirit beings (including Celestines and higher) and every Fera ever are either lying, incompetent or magically coerced/manipulated. And the reason for this seems to be.....because magick exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-22-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:36:02-08:00","id":1053565,"title":"","content":"Entire thread seems to be vampire players expecting werewolf to have the exact same source of angst and despair as VtM. You can absolutely have uncertainty in werewolf, but half the respondents here seem incapable of inserting ambiguity without completely gutting the core of the game, IE, fight a losing war to rebalance the Triat. Making the Garou Nation wrong about everything since year 0 isn't the right way to do it.<br /> <br /> My players have had to make difficult choices, and none of it required me to dangle the possibility of the Wyrm actually being in the right or for Gaia not existing or that their totems have all been hoodwinked by some mage 10,000 years ago. Those don't add anything.<br /> <br /> What if your friends are poisoned by an insidious Wyrm venom? Do you mercy kill them or do you seek out a cure, possibly having to fight your former allies who think your friends should be put down for the good of the sept?<br /> <br /> A kinfolk girl undergoes her first change, but it turns out that she was actually sired by a Black Spiral Dancer... and that there are terrible prophecies about what happens when Whippoorwill claims her as his own. Do you do your best to teach her to stay on the straight and narrow? Do you kill or maim her? Do you banish her into the deep umbra, hoping that distance will stop the bane totem from finding his prey?<br /> <br /> The good and right ruler of the tribal sept is slain in a challenge gone awry, and now your pack's rival and harshest critic is in charge. Will you fall in line, only to get placed in some of the most deadly missions 'to test your mettle,' or will you rebel against the new leader and stage a coup? How close, if at all, will you cleave to the Litany? Are you attempting to seize control yourselves, or just taking down someone wholly unfit to lead?<br /> <br /> And regardless of how and why you do what you do, the Weaver is still ascendant, the Wyrm is completely berserk, and the Wyld is dying but doesn't care. Kinda bleak, really, but you are fighting too hard to notice... and if you stop, the despair of Harano beckons...<br /> <br /> Without getting into gory detail, I think that shit is all pretty nuanced. The Wyrm = bad, Gaia = good, but how her servants act and prosecute the war is still totally up in the air. No need for mind-controlled spirits or vampire conspiracies here, boss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-22-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:27:06-08:00","id":1053582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053565#post1053565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Entire thread seems to be vampire players expecting werewolf to have the exact same source of angst and despair as VtM. You can absolutely have uncertainty in werewolf, but half the respondents here seem incapable of inserting ambiguity without completely gutting the core of the game, IE, fight a losing war to rebalance the Triat. Making the Garou Nation wrong about everything since year 0 isn't the right way to do it.<br /> <br /> My players have had to make difficult choices, and none of it required me to dangle the possibility of the Wyrm actually being in the right or for Gaia not existing or that their totems have all been hoodwinked by some mage 10,000 years ago. Those don't add anything.<br /> <br /> What if your friends are poisoned by an insidious Wyrm venom? Do you mercy kill them or do you seek out a cure, possibly having to fight your former allies who think your friends should be put down for the good of the sept?<br /> <br /> A kinfolk girl undergoes her first change, but it turns out that she was actually sired by a Black Spiral Dancer... and that there are terrible prophecies about what happens when Whippoorwill claims her as his own. Do you do your best to teach her to stay on the straight and narrow? Do you kill or maim her? Do you banish her into the deep umbra, hoping that distance will stop the bane totem from finding his prey?<br /> <br /> The good and right ruler of the tribal sept is slain in a challenge gone awry, and now your pack's rival and harshest critic is in charge. Will you fall in line, only to get placed in some of the most deadly missions 'to test your mettle,' or will you rebel against the new leader and stage a coup? How close, if at all, will you cleave to the Litany? Are you attempting to seize control yourselves, or just taking down someone wholly unfit to lead?<br /> <br /> And regardless of how and why you do what you do, the Weaver is still ascendant, the Wyrm is completely berserk, and the Wyld is dying but doesn't care. Kinda bleak, really, but you are fighting too hard to notice... and if you stop, the despair of Harano beckons...<br /> <br /> Without getting into gory detail, I think that shit is all pretty nuanced. The Wyrm = bad, Gaia = good, but how her servants act and prosecute the war is still totally up in the air. No need for mind-controlled spirits or vampire conspiracies here, boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of great stuff. Especially the example scenarios.<br /> <br /> It's almost like WtA is a completely different game than VtM or MtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T00:54:27-08:00","id":1053685,"title":"","content":"Once again, WtA cannot exist without its lore. If you take all the Gaian myth, all the Wyrm and such, you are left with a gutted shell of a game. You can EASILY play vampire with no Cain or Lillith, as the game is focused on personal trials.<br /> <br /> That is why we are defending it so much, it is very much the reason -why- WtA is liked in the first place. It isn't really a game about werewolves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:42:07-08:00","id":1053704,"title":"","content":"Only having followed this discussion loosely....<br /> <br /> This thread isn't an attack on WtA canon. It's not trying to tell you you should play WtA differently. Or the devs that they should make WtA canon more ambigious.<br /> It's merely some brainstorming about what WtA would be like if a big setting constant weren't as constant anymore. Yes this changes the game, alot. That doesn't make it wrong or a terrible idea. It's cool if you express why you think this is a bad idea, but by now it sounds more like &quot;bah vampire players leave our setting alone&quot;. That's just silly. It's ok if this change seems wrong to you and detracts from the game. Just ignore the thread then, it clearly deals with a topic you have no interest in.<br /> <br /> I personally find the ideas offered here interesting. And the WtA forum is the correct space for this discussion as it is inherently about WtA and not how to adop werewolves to VtM or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T02:13:58-08:00","id":1053717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053704#post1053704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only having followed this discussion loosely....<br /> <br /> This thread isn't an attack on WtA canon. It's not trying to tell you you should play WtA differently. Or the devs that they should make WtA canon more ambigious.<br /> It's merely some brainstorming about what WtA would be like if a big setting constant weren't as constant anymore. Yes this changes the game, alot. That doesn't make it wrong or a terrible idea. It's cool if you express why you think this is a bad idea, but by now it sounds more like &quot;bah vampire players leave our setting alone&quot;. That's just silly. It's ok if this change seems wrong to you and detracts from the game. Just ignore the thread then, it clearly deals with a topic you have no interest in.<br /> <br /> I personally find the ideas offered here interesting. And the WtA forum is the correct space for this discussion as it is inherently about WtA and not how to adop werewolves to VtM or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like I could have posted the &quot;Lilith made the Werewolves and Fera&quot; idea in the VTM forum, and I actually did ages back. It was a big thread on the ways Lilith shaped the Jyhad. It fits well in the VTM lore and it makes them feel more like part of the setting. It makes Werespiders feel less wacky when you can think &quot;okay some fucked up Vampires did this&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I literally chose WTA because it's canon is built up as being impervious, somewhat like Demon, however both are riddled with possibilities for subversion of memory.<br /> <br /> As for those who have commented comparing it to a &quot;it was all a dream&quot; twist, that's only if the storyteller is incompetent. The spirits who tell you how to live your life are the creations of an evil Leech can be an awful twist, or a good twist, depending on how it's delivered, forshadowed and brought into the tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T02:19:40-08:00","id":1053718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053685#post1053685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, WtA cannot exist without its lore. If you take all the Gaian myth, all the Wyrm and such, you are left with a gutted shell of a game. You can EASILY play vampire with no Cain or Lillith, as the game is focused on personal trials.<br /> <br /> That is why we are defending it so much, it is very much the reason -why- WtA is liked in the first place. It isn't really a game about werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does something have to be true to matter? I got into this argument with some Mage players when I suggested that an ST could pick a Paradigm to be the Correct Paradigm behind the scenes as a reflection of the Earthly Foundations.<br /> <br /> &quot;oh, but that makes my character worthless!&quot;<br /> <br /> If you seriously think your character's philosophy, historical beliefs and religion need to be correct for the RP and story to matter, then I don't know what to say. Again, Vampire players knowingly play people who are (probably) incorrect all of the time. And even if a Werewolf finds out that Gaia is a myth constructed to manipulate the Changers, would that make environmentalism worthless? I'm reading this as &quot;oh, the spirits and the Triat are a lie or some kind of trick, I guess everything we've ever done is worthless&quot;. That says a lot, in my opinion. Oddly enough, fighting against pollution is good whether the earth has a spirit which can speak for itself or not. Doing good things is still worthwhile even if the Renown system turns out to be a manipulation.<br /> <br /> The example I'd give is a Bahari who discovers that Lilith was a myth. She wouldn't cry or get angry, since the gifts given to her by those myths matter whether it was &quot;true&quot; or not. &quot;It has to be true to count&quot; is... a very unnuanced look at religion, lore and history. Personally I seriously doubt that the Mysticism of Native Americans is literally correct, and I could say the same for all religion (despite being religious). But hey, weirdly enough I still think respecting the land and showing kindness to strangers and being kind to animals are virtuous things. A Werewolf who gave up fighting corruption, insanity and pollution simply because their Extra Special Religion turned out to be partially or totally incorrect would be a shallow individual I wouldn't have much time for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-23-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T03:14:55-08:00","id":1053729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053718#post1053718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does something have to be true to matter? I got into this argument with some Mage players when I suggested that an ST could pick a Paradigm to be the Correct Paradigm behind the scenes as a reflection of the Earthly Foundations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In WtA, sadly yes. The game literally relies on its lore to function well. Some facts can be false, but given how reliant the game is with how its world works to support its narrative, there really is the need to see it as fact.<br /> <br /> Because, if you take away all the lore, garou are basically shapeshifting creatures with anger issues, spread all around the world. With no apocalypse and with no wyrm, there isn't even the militant religiousness, because that is where that comes from.<br /> <br /> They don't really resemble any mythical werewolves at all, either, since a bite doesn't infect people. And they don't have to shift during the full moon. Becoming one is either due to being born one, or acing at occult and gathering skins of five of them. They are pretty much a fantasy race, like elves or orcs, not a true blue monstrous wolfcreature. You become a mage, ghost or a vampire from a human. A garou is always garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, with no Litany or unified goals, garou can be cannibals relishing on being inhuman and forming their own creation myths. But these are on the personal rather than racial level.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do understand your point about not all myths being true, but garou as monsters doesn't work like it does in vampire. Yes, extreism is bad and cults even moreso. But because being a garou is a (mostly) born condition, it's basically saying that a person is a monster because their ancestors were horrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-23-2017, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:20:05-08:00","id":1053783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053718#post1053718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does something have to be true to matter?<br /> If you seriously think your character's philosophy, historical beliefs and religion need to be correct for the RP and story to matter, then I don't know what to say.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think these two are very interesting and good discussion points in general. I think the value of truth in roleplaying would be a terribly interesting discussion/thing to read about.<br /> <br /> Again, not to be critical, I think it is inherently flawed to compare Vampire and Werewolf in these regards. Vampire is giving you options for a wide area of worldviews, origins, purposes, etc. Your Bahari might find worth in their mindset or the myth of Lilith. But fundamentally that was a choice the character made as well. Mage is doing very much the same thing. The war between Vampire Sects is about ideology, and can be further adjusted with Paths. The war between the Technocracy and Traditions is also about ideology, also tempered by Paradigms.<br /> <br /> A Werewolf isn't choosing to be a Werewolf and they don't really have any other mindset they can adopt. The battle against the Wyrm doesn't leave room for much moral ambiguity (on a broad level). Pentex and the Black Spiral Dancers (broadly) are just evil. It is almost like a bait and switch for Werewolf because the setting, themes, etc are actually seemingly built upon various accepted truths. I think a big degree comes into what changes are being made, obviously. But the purpose for their existence and the nature of the Apocalypse are rather important. It lacks agency if certain things aren't correct.<br /> <br /> Now, I want to take a look at the concept in general. Does something need to be true to matter? No. BUT, I think some value or justification needs to be given to make those experiences matter. Again, I really want to avoid scenarios or specific examples because I know it'll sound unfair. Like I said before, and you said earlier, &quot;As for those who have commented comparing it to a &quot;it was all a dream&quot; twist, that's only if the storyteller is incompetent. The spirits who tell you how to live your life are the creations of an evil Leech can be an awful twist, or a good twist, depending on how it's delivered, forshadowed and brought into the tale.&quot; Most stories can be good or bad depending on how well the ST presents it. The thing is, I think there is a grey area and that this truth versus meaning situation isn't so cut and dry.<br /> <br /> Taking your Bahari as the example, they take meaning in because fundamentally the Path still imposes various philosophical value. Same with something like Native American Mysticism. I'm not sure (and this isn't a knock against them) that the Garou belief system holds the same innate value beyond the purpose it serves. It ends up feeling like a dupe if the character was wrong. I'd arguably say that saying one view of Mage is right can hurt as well, but that'd be a bit specific on the paradigm. Now these things being wrong doesn't mean a character is worthless because they were wrong. But I'd posit that it is inherently less satisfying if their sole worldview and purpose is fundamentally wrong. This is why I think people are suggesting the idea is similar to 'it was all a dream' scenario. It doesn't need to be a stark parity between THIS MATTERS and THIS NO LONGER MATTERS for story and RP. But a gradient of what is enjoyable, typically with people enjoying being right, success, etc. You can lose or be wrong and have fun. But Werewolf isn't presented in a way that easily allows being wrong about certain things and also be quite as fun. People can easily get emotionally invested in that sorta thing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:18:03-08:00","id":1053803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053704#post1053704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's merely some brainstorming about what WtA would be like if a big setting constant weren't as constant anymore. Yes this changes the game, alot. That doesn't make it wrong or a terrible idea. It's cool if you express why you think this is a bad idea, but by now it sounds more like &quot;bah vampire players leave our setting alone&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that this is a &quot;bah vampire players leave our setting alone&quot; sort of thing (worth noting that there is a ton of crossover in the player bases). You have players who are much more familiar with the setting (seemingly) than the OP is trying to explain why such changes to the setting alter the game beyond recognition. The foundation of the setting is particularly important to WtA functioning. Garou and inextricably tied into the greater setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053704#post1053704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's just silly. It's ok if this change seems wrong to you and detracts from the game. Just ignore the thread then, it clearly deals with a topic you have no interest in.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the entire idea of forums is about debate and discussion. The solution you present above is to have anyone who disagrees just gloss over the thread and don't bother speaking up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053717#post1053717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like I could have posted the &quot;Lilith made the Werewolves and Fera&quot; idea in the VTM forum, and I actually did ages back. It was a big thread on the ways Lilith shaped the Jyhad. It fits well in the VTM lore and it makes them feel more like part of the setting. It makes Werespiders feel less wacky when you can think &quot;okay some fucked up Vampires did this&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> In a VtM setting, this interpretation has a lot more leeway since Lupines do not <i>need</i> to be Garou. Fera can used completely free of their lore/background. It is 100% fact that in the WtA setting Ananasi (and Mokole and Rokea) predate humans by hundreds of millions of years. We know this from Setting books. This isn't relying on spirit interpretation to tell us this. This is a truth in the setting of Werewolf. So blaming Ananasi on Vampires having done something wacky doesn't fit into the setting. It just doesn't work because we are told the truth of it by the authors of the Setting. Tons of things in WtA can be left open to interpretation. The fundamentals of the Setting aren't those things because from there everything is built up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053717#post1053717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I literally chose WTA because it's canon is built up as being impervious, somewhat like Demon, however both are riddled with possibilities for subversion of memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't &quot;impervious&quot; to changing. But you have to actually understand how things fit together in order to be able to change them without scrapping the entire setting as written. Quoting the OP from another thread within the last 2 days:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052686-garou-and-vampires?p=1052823#post1052823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but to be fair I've read Changing Breeds but not the Core W20 so I'm missing some key knowledge lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is really the root of the problem with the changes being presented.<br /> <br /> I had more to post but have run out of time and will try and come back to this later in the day.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:26:30-08:00","id":1053809,"title":"","content":"Yes, the entire point of WtA is the Lore. Without the Lore, you do not have WtA, you have furry superheroes with anger issues and an allergy to silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T09:18:35-08:00","id":1053853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does something have to be true to matter? I got into this argument with some Mage players when I suggested that an ST could pick a Paradigm to be the Correct Paradigm behind the scenes as a reflection of the Earthly Foundations.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage, it's important that all Paradigms are equally false or equally true because Mages fight the Ascencion War to set their Paradigm in the throne. If one way it's inherently worse to do so (as the Foundations are supposed to be ludicrously hard to change), it diminishes the stakes. The Traditions are fighting a battle to get their Paradigms accepted when, even if they win, they will still be at odds with Reality(tm) in several fundamental ways. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are in a battle to save the universe. If it's all a lie, then there's no battle to save the universe. Being green may still be right, but the stakes are much less epic.<br /> <br /> I think that the equivalent with Vampire would be to say that the Jyhad it's false. There's no Elders controlling the world in the shadows, there's no vampire of a generation lower than 7 (these are the Antediluvians), and no vampire remembers the ages eons past because the human mind can't contain all that experience, so they invent stories to the young that makes them look more powerful and important than they are. Until the players discover the truth.<br /> <br /> And since everything it's relative and OOC doesn't matter, this it's a valid interpretation of the Lore (because lvl 5 Magic it's more than enough to lie to Neonates), and it's better than vampire lore because it makes you question everything you believed to be true as player.<br /> <br /> \u200bYet this isn't the world the average vampire player bought when joining the table. When you go to play Vampire, you think you're going to play with the setting as presented in the books (more or less).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-23-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T09:48:19-08:00","id":1053857,"title":"","content":"Yes, it would be like an ST recruiting players for a VtM game and, after a few sessions, revealing that the world is actually VtR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:24:09-08:00","id":1053908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053853#post1053853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the equivalent with Vampire would be to say that the Jyhad it's false. There's no Elders controlling the world in the shadows, there's no vampire of a generation lower than 7 (these are the Antediluvians), and no vampire remembers the ages eons past because the human mind can't contain all that experience, so they invent stories to the young that makes them look more powerful and important than they are. Until the players discover the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time of Thin Blood literally endorses &quot;Gehenna is a lie&quot; as one of the possible outcomes of the End Times. It was all a myth, a move in the Jyhad, there's no end of days coming for Vampires, Elders just wake up occasionally but there's no coordination to it.<br /> <br /> What you're suggesting is kind of... shit. Like there's a difference between &quot;setting exists as presented superficially but underneath something different is happening&quot; and &quot;setting exists as presented except when you uncover everything there's nothing there&quot;. Replacing Gaia with Lilith is being falsely made equivalent to replacing all of the history of Vampire before, say 1000 AD with absolutely nothing.<br /> <br /> Also, let's be real, even if the Gaian lore is total bollocks, Pentex are still bastards and there's still good reasons to be green. Werewolves go from being &quot;But Thou Must&quot; eco-warriors who are press-ganged by their families and spirits into fighting for nature into being actual environmentalists who are supporting it for its own sake. Again, I just want to discuss these as alternatives, I'm not saying they're superior or that they should be implemented in favour of the Actual Lore.<br /> <br /> My conclusions are as follows, and I don't think they're controversial ideas at all:<br /> <br /> 1: STs should be open to tweaking, altering or completely subverting the Lore as presented<br /> <br /> 2: Players should be given the space to be skeptical of the Lore both IC and OOC<br /> <br /> 3: Things don't need to be true to be important<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, I'm not even a serious environmentalist and I feel like there's some deep-seated negative implications in the idea that Gaia not existing would make the Garou's plight pointless. I'll do a response to all of the posts I haven't responded to yet at some point, I'm supposed to be doing like 5 essays right now.<br /> <br /> Oh, and yes, I haven't read the Core W20 book. I have, however, read Book of the Wyrm and the Changing Breeds book, and I've read basically all of the lore available on the WW Wiki. I'm feeling an increasingly hostile environment and the responses have varied from thoughtful and interesting to &quot;ugh, you just don't get it&quot;, backed up by generally fallacious assertions and some emotional appeals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:35:16-08:00","id":1053947,"title":"","content":"Sorry for all the long-winded posts, but this is a nice topic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I just want to discuss these as alternatives, I'm not saying they're superior or that they should be implemented in favour of the Actual Lore. </div> </div> </div> Well, with all due respect, your OP gave that impression a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that this is true, or that it should be true. I'm trying to make a comment on the<b> nature of lore and how we should use it</b>. I'm trying to point out why in-universe and out-of-universe skepticism of the status quo <b>should be given more time and space</b>. </div> </div> </div> I agree discussing alternatives can be good. Even the idea that alternatives CAN exist seems fine. But your posts did (just a tiny, tiny, tiny bit) come off as saying This Is Good, This Is How Lore Should Be Used. Some people do want hard setting facts and truths. Some people fundamentally enjoy a more firm setting as far as lore goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My conclusions are as follows, and I don't think they're controversial ideas at all:<br /> 1: STs should be open to tweaking, altering or completely subverting the Lore as presented </div> </div> </div>I entirely agree, if that's there desire for the game they want to run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: Players should be given the space to be skeptical of the Lore both IC and OOC </div> </div> </div> I generally agree in the same vein as the above. But I personally think having at least a vague understanding of the setting and certain aspects of the lore is important between players and their ST (yes, it'll vary based on taste and trust levels). Which is kind of the reason I think a lot of people still enjoy so much about cWoD. While tweaking has been encouraged and the metaplot backed off in the X20 series, I think a lot of people fundamentally enjoy what the world of darkness is. There is a level of comfort in knowing what you are getting. I would just say to be aware that some people do prefer their setting to be more concrete and determined when they set out. Not everyone enjoys the same level of skepticism IC/OOC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Things don't need to be true to be important </div> </div> </div> This seems the most unfair to me and I think is the main issue people are having with the entire premise. While I generally agree with the first two, people can enjoy their own thing. If someone only cares about their character/RP if said character is right in regards to certain assumptions, that's what they want. That's their thing. I personally agree enjoyment can be found whether or not certain things are real. After all, this is roleplaying, it is all basically mental pretend-work. But it still seems a tad judgmental to expect others to have fun in the same way. I personally do prefer assuming my (and my character's) world-views are true, or at least partial true. Something about that is just more enjoyable to me. Though I find it hard to explain why. This is just a personal preference thing and I don't think assuming others will feel the same way is a good starting point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean seriously, I'm not even a serious environmentalist and I feel like there's some deep-seated negative implications in the idea that Gaia not existing would make the Garou's plight pointless </div> </div> </div> Again, I think there is a big gradient between something being super meaningful and outright pointless when it comes to enjoying playing a character. The whiplash response of, 'my character is now meaningless,' is seemingly an exaggeration (not that I doubt some have stated that explicitly), but it reduces the point. It can be as simple as, 'I enjoy my character more when his beliefs are true or unconfirmed.' That seems like an extremely fair statement to me, if that's what someone likes. And I think it plays into why people dig into WoD canon so much at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:42:02-08:00","id":1053955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixiekillerEin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053480#post1053480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see you take the Fallout 3 aproach to player choice and morality</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I take the World of Darkness approach to choice and morality.<br /> <br /> When given the oppertunity to repent by God, Caine chose to scorn the offer and keeps scorning it to this date. Vampires choose to be monsters lest monsters they become.<br /> As difficult as it can be, the Garou choose to fight a near-hopeless battle against the Wyrm.<br /> Mages choose, and try to impose their choice onto the world.<br /> When a Wraith chooses to not let its memories of life hold it back it can truly move on.<br /> Faeries choose to bring back wonder and awe to a world overflowing with cynicism and banality.<br /> Hunters choose to act when others cower or hesitate, which leads to them being Imbued.<br /> Mummies choose to take the fight to Apophis for the sake of the world.<br /> Demons are the choice between subservience to God and living on one's own terms. Because if God had made humanity sapient to begin with, the sapience would have no meaning.<br /> <br /> Having choice is meaningless when it is made before you. Why else do you think the Most High ordered Lucifer to start a rebellion? He did what he was told and through that gave both the angels and humanity something they never had before: true choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:02:21-08:00","id":1053969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1053955#post1053955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I take the World of Darkness approach to choice and morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the choice is:<br /> <br /> A: Be on the side of justice, even if it's hard and you might lose<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> B: Literally worship the insane force of destruction which is tipping the world towards the apocalypse, while indulging the most disgusting and carnal desires you can imagine (torture, rape, incest, cannibalism)<br /> <br /> Then it's Fallout 3 Morality. Just take a look at the mission where the only choice is to either set off a Nuke for no reason whatsoever, or disarm it. Or the famously awful ending where you can choose to wipe out all Ghouls &quot;because ugly&quot; or, well, not do that.<br /> <br /> There is room for individuals who are truly wrong and truly evil, but there's a reason why such groups have become rarer as time went on. Look at 1st edition.<br /> <br /> Technocracy: &quot;Mwahahahah!&quot; *twirls moustache*<br /> Sabbat: &quot;Mwahahahaha! All Hail the Demons! Diablerie for all!&quot;<br /> <br /> And you know what happened to those groups as the game-lines progressed? They got Nuanced. The Technocracy literally saved the world when they killed [Ravnos]. And they are set up so that someone with different views from me, but a reasonable person, could support them if they existed without being a monster. The Sabbat are still terrible and gross, but they don't worship demons and they have a realistic edge to them, they feel like something people might do if they became Vampires, and there are ways to play it which are nuanced and interesting, and their failings are a brilliant thing to explore (yes, 1000 years and not a step closer to either of your goals, well done).<br /> <br /> From what I've read, WTA has some awesome and interesting antagonists available to it. The Ratkin and the Ananasi can easily be antagonists and can be done well. Vampires can be cool villains. Pentex is something I can imagine people supporting in real life, not good people, but I can see it existing and functioning. The Spiral Dancers? It feels a bit... 1st writeup Baali. A bit 1st edition Sabbat. You've already got mindless Wyrmish monsters. Couldn't we give them a legitimate philosophy? So the reason they become so depraved and do so much terrible stuff is because their goal as a Tribe is to rescue the Wyrm from its Frenzy (with them believing that the Wyrm is 100% sane, it's simply gone into a Werewolf-like Frenzy and being a member of the Triat it's lasting a seriously long period of time since they exist on a larger scale). They believe that if they can delve deep enough into the mindset of destruction they can find the key to rescuing it. They walk the spiral, and then they walk back up the spiral to sanity. They do it over and over until they (hopefully, one day) reach the level of the Wyrm's frenzy and manage to walk back from it. At that point they'll know how to save the Wyrm. And THEY CAN BE WRONG. They can have been fooled by the Wyrm who is 100% aware of its actions. They can have been manipulated by the Ananasi or by banes or by a potent Elder Vampire. They can simply have listened to the doctrine of a fool. At least this way there is some reason (at least at first) to their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-23-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:37:45-08:00","id":1054018,"title":"","content":"My problem with a lot of the arguments saying that WtA Lore has to be accurate for various reasons seem to be forgetting things. One argument is that because they work with spirits regularly and cultivate relationships with them that they have the spirits to fall back on for explaining why they are right. I feel that they are forgetting that spirits are beings with their own perspective of the world and agendas so for all anyone knows they could be lying to the Changing Breeds or only giving half truths that are only partially true that the Garou have taken and twisted into a religion of their own.<br /> <br /> Other arguments are that because there are beings like the Rokea, Mokole, and Ratkin with memories going back thousands or more years ago are proof but again memories aren't exactly known to be reliable. Demons are far older than any of those beings so by that logic they have more proof than any Changing Breed that their view of things are correct but if the accuracy of their memory is up to debate then why shouldn't Changing Breeds'? It could be argued that they are simply more confident in their memories than Demons but there isn't real proof that they are right. Speaking of DtF, their Lore outright contradicts WtA Lore so why should WtA be considered more accurate? While there is more ambiguity in DtF than there is in WtA there is no good reason to say that WtA Lore should taken as absolute just because of the thought that without their Lore then they are meaningless. This is the World of Darkness, it would fit that they are creatures who are ultimately fighting a meaningless war because of religious beliefs that have no real foundation.<br /> <br /> All that said, in a pure Werewolf game I would treat it as accurate but I would still add ambiguity to it like questioning whether they are really serving their purpose as was truly intended by Gaia or have they twisted things to justify their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:38:52-08:00","id":1054019,"title":"","content":"No, the BSD give up on anything good and sane by walking the spiral. There are heroic BSDs who heroically resist their Tribe and the Wyrm by running away before they are forced to walk the Spiral. They either join the other Garou in the fight against the Wyrm, join the Ahadi or Beast Courts in the fight against the Wyrm, or just become Ronin. They become incapable of resisting when they walk the Spiral because they choose to align with the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> And what proof do Demons have other than the memories that conflict with reality? Kindred and Fera did not exist when Demons were imprisoned, according to the Demons themselves, but even Demons do not know what effect the corruption of the Abyss had on their memories. For all they know, 'God' took their true memories and replaced them with lies as part of their punishment for their rebellion. After all, Demons are creatures of lies according to most mythologies, so it would be appropriate of even their memories are lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-23-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:56:28-08:00","id":1054030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054019#post1054019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what proof do Demons have other than the memories that conflict with reality? Kindred and Fera did not exist when Demons were imprisoned, according to the Demons themselves, but even Demons do not know what effect the corruption of the Abyss had on their memories. For all they know, 'God' took their true memories and replaced them with lies as part of their punishment for their rebellion. After all, Demons are creatures of lies according to most mythologies, so it would be appropriate of even their memories are lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what proof is there that it is all lies? While it is left ambiguous unlike in WtA, it is just as possible that the Changing Breeds are simply overconfident in their beliefs. You don't have to go far to find people who are absolutely certain that the stories in the bible reflect a true history of the wold and that the world is only 6000 years old and will say their evidence is personal revelation. Kindred and Fera didn't exist when they were imprisoned but humans did which invalidates at least the Mokole Lore. On top of that WtA Lore states that the world was created by the combined efforts of the Triat yet DtF Lore outright says that it was created by God through Angels. From the DtF perspective Fera could just be creations of Earthbound. My point is that just because Lore defines a game doesn't mean that Lore should always be treated as objectively accurate. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:14:00-08:00","id":1054041,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Demon Lore is ambiguous, but the Werewolf Lore is not. Since this is the Werewolf forum, the objective nature of Werewolf Lore is respected (in Demon games, feel free to toss Werewolf Lore aside). In WtA, Demons are just deluded Wyrm spirits with pretentious of greatness that were released from their ancient prison by the events of the Week of Nightmares. <br /> <br /> While the exact WtA interpretation of their nature of Demons is up for debate, my theory is as follows. Demons were High Umbra spirits corrupted by the Wyrm. When their corruption reached a certain point, they rebelled against the Godhead of the High Umbra. When they were defeated by the loyalists of the Godhead of the High Umbra, they were cast into Oblivion, where they were consumed and digested by Grandmother before She shat their corrupted remains into the Abyss, Her personal toilet for anything that Her Oblivion could not destroy (the nutrition provided to Her by digesting the proto-Demons allowed Her to create the True Malfeans). When Grandmother moved, She weakened the seals that She maintained on the Abyss, allowing the weakest Demons to escape and do the work of the Wyrm by possessing humans and spreading their corruption through the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:14:30-08:00","id":1054327,"title":"","content":"Like I said, in a pure WtA game I keep them as being accurate but like to have ambiguity as to whether they are fully right or if they have twisted it in some way to justify their own agendas.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity though, in a mixed game do you think that they should still be treated objectively accurate about their beliefs? Because say for example Mage without the consensus is just as much of a gut as Werewolf without its Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:56:07-08:00","id":1054341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time of Thin Blood literally endorses &quot;Gehenna is a lie&quot; as one of the possible outcomes of the End Times. It was all a myth, a move in the Jyhad, there's no end of days coming for Vampires, Elders just wake up occasionally but there's no coordination to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Jyhad still exist there, and vampires are still gothic monsters ploting in an endless war of the ages...if Garou are created by Lilith to kill vampires, and she subverted all the Spirit World to do that, then the war against the Apocalypse takes a step back to the Jyhad, the Wyrm it's not the main antagonist, but a pawn of Lilith. More so, the Garou stop to be sacred spiritual warriors to become environmentalists, which it's no small change of theme, even if being green if good.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, I'm propossing to make the Jyhad a non issue to vampires. Not merely to take away the Antediluvians who aren't important to the players until the Gehena, but to take the main reason to fight. Just as in Mage the main reason to fight it's to control or protect Reality itself, fighting for the souls of humanity, in vampire the main reason to fight it's the promisse of power and the paranoia of the world of the undead (impersonated in the Elders, with their milenia old schemes)<br /> <br /> You can still fight to gain power as a vampire if the milenia old schemes don't exist. The Sabbat exists the Camarilla exists, they're not terribly powerful, but there are reasons to be involved in the conflict, mainly that you were born in it. And you can still advance your vampiric power and status, just not to the godly level of 7 gen and above (which are levels that most players never see anyway).<br /> <br /> But vampire losses it's apeal without the milenia old schemes, doesn't it? . Same goes for Mage if mages can't do shit to change the world in which we live, because what science knows it's and will always be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you're suggesting is kind of... shit. Like there's a difference between &quot;setting exists as presented superficially but underneath something different is happening&quot; and &quot;setting exists as presented except when you uncover everything there's nothing there&quot;. Replacing Gaia with Lilith is being falsely made equivalent to replacing all of the history of Vampire before, say 1000 AD with absolutely nothing. </div> </div> </div>To my undertanding &quot;<b>setting exists</b> as presented <b>except</b> <b>when you uncover everything there's nothing there</b>&quot; and &quot;<b>setting exists</b> as presented <b>superficially but underneath something different is happening</b>&quot; are very similar in the sense that <i>if &quot;something different from the setting it's all that it's happening&quot; then &quot;nothing of the setting it's there&quot;</i>. You've just killed the setting, and replaced it with other thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My conclusions are as follows, and I don't think they're controversial ideas at all:<br /> <br /> 1: STs should be open to tweaking, altering or completely subverting the Lore as presented<br /> <br /> 2: Players should be given the space to be skeptical of the Lore both IC and OOC<br /> <br /> 3: Things don't need to be true to be important </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with the first 2, but not with the 3.<br /> <br /> Truth it's important as long as truth it's meaningfull to the choices players make in the game. If the piece of lore you're &quot;debunking&quot; it's distant, then it doesn't matter because it will hardly enter in play, and only as a wierd mystery, but if it's close and personal it can disrupt the spirit of the game.<br /> <br /> Now, disrupting the spirit can be good...some people like to play Vampions, some people might enjoy a Vampire more dawn to earth like the one I propossed, without low generations and milenia old plots...if your players agree, change it's good. This generates a conundrum, because if you want the big reveal to be a surprise you need to lie to the players(they think they're about to fight the Wyrm as Gaia's chosen, and they're going to play Lupine: the Lilim).<br /> <br /> Now, let me ask you this:<br /> <br /> Why someone that defends that truth isn't important needs to defend his point of view as a &quot;valid way to use/understad the lore&quot; instead of a drastic deviation the lore, an interprtation instead of a house rule? Why do you need your new lore to be something diffrent from changing the rules?<br /> <br /> Why do you need OOC to be universaly relative in order to play the game the way you want?<br /> <br /> I think that the answers would have been much less &quot;negative&quot; if you had presented your proposition as a brainstorm to study what happens if you change the setting in a certain way, instead of the best way to use the lore that makes perfect sense within the setting. Because the latter it's calling to people that may think that:<br /> A. It isn't the best way to use the lore<br /> B. It doesn't make perfect sense within the setting<br /> C. You're ignoring the lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-24-2017, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:58:49-08:00","id":1054343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054327#post1054327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity though, in a mixed game do you think that they should still be treated objectively accurate about their beliefs? Because say for example Mage without the consensus is just as much of a gut as Werewolf without its Lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a mixed game you have to decide how you want the cosmologies and lore to line up. They just kind of don't without changes. Usually the ST is tasked with choosing one game as the&quot;base&quot; and building off of that. <br /> <br /> Unless the game gets too the upper levels of power, the bulk of the conflicts can be kept hidden and never addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:45:23-08:00","id":1054351,"title":"","content":"Yup.<br /> <br /> The problem of truth, obviously, only comes arround if something it's revealed to be, indeed, true beyond reasonable doubt.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this it's a perfect ocation to ilustrate the diffeence between IOC and OOC. IOC a Mage can say whatever he wants, no Garou (nor Werewolf player) it's going to buy it (or maybe he does, Garou aren't a hive mind). The Big Book of Crossover that explains who it's trully the Big bad of WoD and which faction trully Rules the Night, on the other hand, it's going to upset a lot of fans because it's the Word of God. Personally, I think you could do a Small Book of Crossover that's just rules, without revealing anything, that would still be of great use to fans of crossover, but well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:09:14-08:00","id":1054403,"title":"","content":"I think that it also depends on the Mage. The members of the Mythic Traditions (Cult of Ecstasy, Dreamspeakers, Order of Hermes, and Verbena) will shrug at the idea of the WtA Lore being the objective truth because it does not interfere with their way of doing True Magick (and it might actually address some of their questions about the nature of Reality). The members of the Mythic Traditions are not focused on the idea of subjective reality because the Mythic Traditions tend to be built around mystical rules and prohibitions that tend to align well with the WtA Lore. The Mages that have the most problems with the WtA Lore are the members of the Technocratic Union because their entire purpose is the twist the Consensus to the point where they can run reality without the interference of supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> In a mixed Mage-Werewolf game, it probably works best if the Mage Lore is a subjective interpretation of Werewolf Lore (otherwise the Fera just end up being fuzzy superheroes with anger issues and silver allergies). The Technocrats are the unwitting servants of the Weaver, manipulated by the Weaver to strengthen the Pattern by destroying the creativity and magic of Human existence. The Nephandi are the willing servants of the Wyrm, even if they claim to serve independent evils, because the inversion of their Avatars is caused by Walking the Spiral. The Marauders have been infected with the madness of the Wyld, and their madness compels them to attack the agents of the Wyrm and the agents of the Weaver. The Traditions and the Crafts might be potential allies of the Fera and Gaia, but they might also be unwitting servants of the Weaver, the Wyld, or the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The battles that Mages fight then tend to be as cosmic as the battles that the Fera fight, the Mages just are unwilling to admit that they could endanger all of existence if they fail. Without an instinctive purpose, Mages are distrusted by the Fera because they are the free agents of the cosmic conflict, and are just as likely to sign on with the enemies of the Fera as they would with the Fera. Mages can also cause problems for the Fera by helping the Weaver by destroying the creativity and magic of Human existence through their own blindness or by helping the Wyrm by spreading corruption and misery through their greed and pride. It also does not help that Mages occasionally attack Caerns in order to drain them of their magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:34:12-08:00","id":1054445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054351#post1054351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally, I think you could do a Small Book of Crossover that's just rules, without revealing anything, that would still be of great use to fans of crossover, but well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I don't know that I would have high hopes for this theoretical book. The systems for crossovers that have been published so far are generally rubbish (the comparing power levels rule for example almost always favors Vampires who steamroll all of the other splats nonsensically). I wholly support the idea though of completely leaving fluff out of it and focusing on rules alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:53:19-08:00","id":1054453,"title":"","content":"That would be interesting. I think that it would be good to have a form of universal countermagic rule. I think that just giving major supernatural creatures the two types of Counterspells and the two types of Unweaving for free from Sorcerer: Revised (p. 63) would be adequate for a universal countermagic rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:25:19-08:00","id":1054793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054041#post1054041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Demon Lore is ambiguous, but the Werewolf Lore is not. Since this is the Werewolf forum, the objective nature of Werewolf Lore is respected (in Demon games, feel free to toss Werewolf Lore aside).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know that this is how you think Aya. Next time that you question something about Mage, like when you tryed to IMPOSE rules from Changelling the Dreaming over the Mage scenario, I'll let you remember of this.<br /> <br /> But I do have to agree with the WtA players here; it's not that the Garou char will become useless if you make their Lore utterly wrong; but it's not Werewolf: the Apocalypse game anymore. You could play &quot;Werewolf: the Lie&quot; or &quot;Werewolf: the deception&quot; if you'd like, but it wouldn't be THE APOCALIPSE any more.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that EVERY single piece of the lore MUST be the absolutely ultimate truth; the BSD could have some redeemable qualities or some utter reasons beyond just &quot;evil Nefandi/Baali-like&quot; sort of fellows, the whole thing about &quot;the world is fucked up! Run to the hills, it's over man, it's over!&quot; could be just an exaggeration, and similar things. But, Gaia must be a thing, even if it's not EXACTLY what the Garou think it is (maybe Gaia is utterly evil? Maybe the Weaver could make a world FAR BETTER if given the chance? Maybe the one imprisoning the Wyrm is Gaia, not the Weaver, and if you could release the Wyrm from Gaia, all would be well again?)<br /> <br /> However, just DESTROYING the lore of WtA (like saying &quot;sorry guys, there is no Gaia, it was all a Lucifer's plot all along) is totally undoing the game.<br /> <br /> Like others have said, it would be like Mage without the Consensus, or like Vampire without the Jyhad, or Changelling without the Banality, or Wraith without the Oblivion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:30:11-08:00","id":1054796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054403#post1054403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it also depends on the Mage. The members of the Mythic Traditions (Cult of Ecstasy, Dreamspeakers, Order of Hermes, and Verbena) will shrug at the idea of the WtA Lore being the objective truth because it does not interfere with their way of doing True Magick (and it might actually address some of their questions about the nature of Reality). The members of the Mythic Traditions are not focused on the idea of subjective reality because the Mythic Traditions tend to be built around mystical rules and prohibitions that tend to align well with the WtA Lore. The Mages that have the most problems with the WtA Lore are the members of the Technocratic Union because their entire purpose is the twist the Consensus to the point where they can run reality without the interference of supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> In a mixed Mage-Werewolf game, it probably works best if the Mage Lore is a subjective interpretation of Werewolf Lore (otherwise the Fera just end up being fuzzy superheroes with anger issues and silver allergies). The Technocrats are the unwitting servants of the Weaver, manipulated by the Weaver to strengthen the Pattern by destroying the creativity and magic of Human existence. The Nephandi are the willing servants of the Wyrm, even if they claim to serve independent evils, because the inversion of their Avatars is caused by Walking the Spiral. The Marauders have been infected with the madness of the Wyld, and their madness compels them to attack the agents of the Wyrm and the agents of the Weaver. The Traditions and the Crafts might be potential allies of the Fera and Gaia, but they might also be unwitting servants of the Weaver, the Wyld, or the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The battles that Mages fight then tend to be as cosmic as the battles that the Fera fight, the Mages just are unwilling to admit that they could endanger all of existence if they fail. Without an instinctive purpose, Mages are distrusted by the Fera because they are the free agents of the cosmic conflict, and are just as likely to sign on with the enemies of the Fera as they would with the Fera. Mages can also cause problems for the Fera by helping the Weaver by destroying the creativity and magic of Human existence through their own blindness or by helping the Wyrm by spreading corruption and misery through their greed and pride. It also does not help that Mages occasionally attack Caerns in order to drain them of their magical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that was quickly.<br /> <br /> This is the point were I remember YOU that WtA lore doesn't mean ANYTHING in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> So, no, no objective reality of WtA for a Mage game (just remember your very direct approach of how the lore of Demon doesn't apply for WtA, and please use the same approach when refering to Mage)<br /> <br /> And, it's funny how you managed to destroy the entire scenario of Mage just to preserve your prefered game of WtA.<br /> <br /> If you wanna a good way to have a compromise that could work well in a crossed mage-werewolf game, take a look at the discussions of Consensus on here <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality/page4\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-reality/page4</a><br /> <br /> But, once again, for a pure WtA game, just take the lore as written","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-25-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:31:19-08:00","id":1054838,"title":"","content":"This is a WtA forum, so WtA Lore is going to take precedence over MtAc Lore in a Mage-Werewolf crossover. If anyone wants to discuss a Werewolf-Mage crossover where MtAc Lore takes precedence over WtA Lore, I would suggest that they post a thread on the Mage forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T02:04:49-08:00","id":1055140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1052659-no-you-really-are-just-a-monster-reflection-on-the-nature-of-lore?p=1054838#post1054838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a WtA forum, so WtA Lore is going to take precedence over MtAc Lore in a Mage-Werewolf crossover. If anyone wants to discuss a Werewolf-Mage crossover where MtAc Lore takes precedence over WtA Lore, I would suggest that they post a thread on the Mage forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I do hope you remember those exact words when you post on the Mage forum too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}